WEBVTT

1
00:00:32,857 --> 00:00:34,736
I thought it was good.

2
00:00:34,736 --> 00:00:38,828
I'm not saying that the movie wasn't
good, it was, I enjoyed it, just...

3
00:00:38,828 --> 00:00:41,457
heist movies aren't really
my thing.

4
00:00:41,457 --> 00:00:43,128
I know, I know. I forgot,

5
00:00:43,128 --> 00:00:45,550
you're more of a... you're more
of a romcom girl.

6
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:46,927
I am not.

7
00:00:46,927 --> 00:00:48,556
Grace, I've known you since
you were 14,

8
00:00:48,556 --> 00:00:50,601
you love romcoms more
than anyone I know.

9
00:00:50,601 --> 00:00:53,816
I don’t know if it’s that.
I think it's just...

10
00:00:53,816 --> 00:00:57,364
I like the idea of two people deciding
that they're better off together

11
00:00:57,364 --> 00:00:59,911
than they are apart...
and a happy ending

12
00:00:59,911 --> 00:01:01,665
Ergo, you love romcoms.

13
00:01:01,665 --> 00:01:03,711
Okay, fine.

14
00:01:04,253 --> 00:01:06,341
I got to get back to the office
to do some work,

15
00:01:06,341 --> 00:01:08,219
but I had such a great time.

16
00:01:08,219 --> 00:01:10,474
- Yeah, yeah.
- Yeah.

17
00:01:10,474 --> 00:01:14,315
I guess until the next time one
of us needs a plus one.

18
00:01:14,315 --> 00:01:15,818
Mm, sure.

19
00:01:18,198 --> 00:01:19,868
You're a good friend, Quinn.

20
00:01:19,868 --> 00:01:23,416
- Have a good night, Grace.
- You too.

21
00:01:35,858 --> 00:01:37,529
Yes, we're doing the eggshells shiplap

22
00:01:37,529 --> 00:01:40,242
on the far wall to match the Carrera
marble in the kitchen.

23
00:01:40,242 --> 00:01:43,289
Mm, I'll pick up the backsplash
samples later today.

24
00:01:45,837 --> 00:01:48,676
That is not our job. Sorry.

25
00:01:48,676 --> 00:01:50,972
Uh-huh, I look forward to
the design coming together too.

26
00:01:50,972 --> 00:01:52,767
Chat soon.

27
00:01:52,767 --> 00:01:55,397
Hey, did you finish the mood
boards for Hannah’s tree?

28
00:01:55,397 --> 00:01:57,484
Yeah, I sure did, I have them
back at the office.

29
00:01:57,484 --> 00:02:00,365
Oh, amazing. Listen, I am swamped today,
would you mind running them over to her?

30
00:02:00,365 --> 00:02:02,035
- Yeah, you got it.
- Thank you.

31
00:02:02,035 --> 00:02:04,583
Can we get three hot chocolates, please?

32
00:02:04,958 --> 00:02:06,461
Great. Yes.

33
00:02:06,461 --> 00:02:07,839
What's that?

34
00:02:07,839 --> 00:02:13,308
Ooh. Operation “Complete Jack’s Baseball
Card Collection” is now... well, complete.

35
00:02:13,308 --> 00:02:15,103
Complete as in?

36
00:02:15,103 --> 00:02:18,944
Complete as in, on Christmas morning,
he's going to wake up to every rookie card

37
00:02:18,944 --> 00:02:20,238
from the year he was born.

38
00:02:20,238 --> 00:02:21,658
You’re too good to him.

39
00:02:21,658 --> 00:02:23,077
- You know I love a mission.

40
00:02:23,077 --> 00:02:24,581
I know you do.
Oh, did you see the email?

41
00:02:24,581 --> 00:02:28,046
I did, yeah, the one about us decorating
the Town Square Christmas tree

42
00:02:28,046 --> 00:02:29,381
in less than three days?

43
00:02:29,381 --> 00:02:31,637
Hey, come on, we can do it.
We've done bigger jobs than that,

44
00:02:31,637 --> 00:02:33,348
and that was less notice,
less time.

45
00:02:33,348 --> 00:02:35,645
Yeah. I mean, I guess since
we didn't get the full decorating

46
00:02:35,645 --> 00:02:36,855
contract from Sami...

47
00:02:36,855 --> 00:02:38,567
She wants us to call her Mayor
Hoffman now.

48
00:02:38,567 --> 00:02:41,072
Oh, yeah, of course. It's so weird that
she's our mayor.

49
00:02:41,072 --> 00:02:43,536
I mean, we're the same age,
that just makes me feel old.

50
00:02:43,536 --> 00:02:46,625
I know, but hey, she threw us a bone by
getting us that contract on the tree,

51
00:02:46,625 --> 00:02:48,921
so we should at least try
to call her by her official title.

52
00:02:48,921 --> 00:02:51,969
Yeah, and in the email that I saw,
she's gonna provide all these city

53
00:02:51,969 --> 00:02:53,179
employees to help us out.

54
00:02:53,179 --> 00:02:54,306
We don't need that.

55
00:02:54,306 --> 00:02:56,520
I think we need all the hands
we can get.

56
00:02:57,062 --> 00:02:58,649
Yeah, maybe you're right, but you know
what?

57
00:02:58,649 --> 00:03:03,241
If we pull this off, next year,
the entire town Ivy Glen

58
00:03:03,241 --> 00:03:05,580
could be designed and decorated
by Keen and Rankin.

59
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:06,748
That would be...

60
00:03:06,748 --> 00:03:09,044
Everything we dreamed of when
we started our business!

61
00:03:09,044 --> 00:03:10,088
- Yes! It is, yes.
- I know!

62
00:03:10,088 --> 00:03:11,340
Holy cricket!

63
00:03:11,925 --> 00:03:14,931
Oh, stop that! Just leave it!

64
00:03:39,021 --> 00:03:40,775
<i>Ryan St. Nicholas.</i>

65
00:03:40,775 --> 00:03:42,027
You sound so official.

66
00:03:44,365 --> 00:03:46,077
So do you, Madame Mayor.

67
00:03:46,077 --> 00:03:49,124
How goes your reign in our quaint
hometown?

68
00:03:49,124 --> 00:03:53,759
It's been better. I'm actually calling
to ask you a favour... from an old friend.

69
00:03:53,759 --> 00:03:55,095
<i>What's up?</i>

70
00:03:55,095 --> 00:03:56,263
The St. Nicholas House.

71
00:03:56,263 --> 00:03:57,725
My grandmother's house?

72
00:03:58,059 --> 00:03:59,353
You still own it, right?

73
00:03:59,353 --> 00:04:00,981
For now, yes. Why?

74
00:04:00,981 --> 00:04:03,779
Um... I have a bit of
a situation.

75
00:04:03,779 --> 00:04:06,367
So, Ivy Glen's charities are
in a bit of a pinch.

76
00:04:06,367 --> 00:04:08,454
Normally, Christmas time
is our busiest time,

77
00:04:08,454 --> 00:04:12,129
but now, donating is down
over 50 percent.

78
00:04:12,129 --> 00:04:14,383
Inflation, recession,
everyone's feeling the pinch.

79
00:04:15,135 --> 00:04:18,767
Which doesn't look good for
a young first-term mayor.

80
00:04:19,101 --> 00:04:21,898
Or someone who cares about
their hometown.

81
00:04:23,401 --> 00:04:26,365
Look, it's affecting so many
organizations, especially the food bank.

82
00:04:27,033 --> 00:04:29,622
<i>I wouldn't ask if it wasn't an
emergency, but...</i>

83
00:04:29,622 --> 00:04:33,296
have you considered reviving your
grandmother's Ribbons and Bows Fundraiser?

84
00:04:33,296 --> 00:04:35,718
- Uh...

85
00:04:36,135 --> 00:04:38,181
I don't know, not really
in my wheelhouse.

86
00:04:38,557 --> 00:04:40,143
Even if it would so much good

87
00:04:40,143 --> 00:04:42,774
<i>for the town and honour your family's
tradition?</i>

88
00:04:42,774 --> 00:04:44,569
Okay, okay.

89
00:04:44,569 --> 00:04:47,825
I'll... I'll consider it. I...

90
00:04:47,825 --> 00:04:50,080
was thinking about coming back home
for the holidays

91
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:53,085
anyway to tie up a few things.

92
00:04:53,085 --> 00:04:56,300
Well, let me know as soon as you can,
please, I'm on a bit of a timeline.

93
00:04:56,300 --> 00:04:58,137
Oh, will do, Sami.

94
00:04:58,137 --> 00:05:00,141
I believe that's Mayor
Hoffman to you.

95
00:05:00,141 --> 00:05:03,231
Oh, sorry, Madame Mayor.

96
00:05:12,374 --> 00:05:13,877
Kayla?
<i>- Yes?</i>

97
00:05:13,877 --> 00:05:16,006
Will you book me that flight
back to Ivy Glen?

98
00:05:16,006 --> 00:05:17,300
<i>Of course.</i>

99
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:19,471
I think I’m going to head home
for Christmas after all.

100
00:05:19,471 --> 00:05:21,016
<i>Right away.</i>

101
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:35,169
That was a long cocoa run.

102
00:05:35,169 --> 00:05:39,386
Well, I had to complete operation "Make
Christmas magical for my husband."

103
00:05:39,386 --> 00:05:42,643
- So, you found my race car?
- Yeah, and the track to go with it.

104
00:05:42,643 --> 00:05:43,854
Hi.

105
00:05:43,854 --> 00:05:47,193
Mom called, said she and dad arrived in
Italy and are having a great time.

106
00:05:47,193 --> 00:05:50,993
Told me to tell you she got the fabric
samples from...

107
00:05:50,993 --> 00:05:53,247
- Giuseppe?
- Giuseppe, yeah. Who's Giuseppe?

108
00:05:53,247 --> 00:05:55,209
That's amazing. He is a draper in
Tuscany

109
00:05:55,209 --> 00:05:57,422
and he hand-weaves all these
intricate patterns.

110
00:05:57,422 --> 00:06:00,638
I wanted to use the samples for the mood
boards on the Balzerini’s living room

111
00:06:00,638 --> 00:06:03,142
so that I can tie in their heritage
to the new space.

112
00:06:03,142 --> 00:06:05,606
- Great.
- Yes! I love that.

113
00:06:05,606 --> 00:06:06,983
All right here.

114
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:10,365
Ooh, but we should probably focus on
the Christmas tree design.

115
00:06:10,365 --> 00:06:13,371
Okay. I was thinking lots of lights.

116
00:06:13,371 --> 00:06:16,503
Lights, okay.

117
00:06:16,503 --> 00:06:18,214
Love it. What else?

118
00:06:18,966 --> 00:06:20,468
That's as far as I got.

119
00:06:20,886 --> 00:06:22,640
Okay.

120
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:24,519
Ahh...

121
00:06:24,519 --> 00:06:26,313
Hm...

122
00:06:26,313 --> 00:06:31,115
Well, let me give it some thought.

123
00:06:31,115 --> 00:06:32,785
Where are you going?
We just got here.

124
00:06:32,785 --> 00:06:35,624
Yes, well, I need inspiration.

125
00:06:35,624 --> 00:06:38,505
So, I'll see you both later.

126
00:06:40,341 --> 00:06:43,389
- Bye, sis.
- Good luck. I'll see you soon.

127
00:06:43,389 --> 00:06:46,730
So, about that race car...

128
00:06:46,730 --> 00:06:49,902
Okay, no peeking.
No before Christmas.

129
00:07:27,268 --> 00:07:30,776
Hey, Maggie.
Yes, I saw your email.

130
00:07:31,694 --> 00:07:35,201
Yeah. No, I... I'm in Ivy Glen
as we speak.

131
00:07:36,245 --> 00:07:40,169
I will get the house all set up and
we should be ready to list in a few days.

132
00:07:42,132 --> 00:07:43,802
Uh... I gotta go.

133
00:07:45,096 --> 00:07:47,308
No way.

134
00:07:47,810 --> 00:07:50,732
- I'm... so sorry. Um...

135
00:07:50,732 --> 00:07:52,653
Ryan?

136
00:07:52,653 --> 00:07:53,822
Grace.

137
00:07:53,822 --> 00:07:56,285
Hi. What...

138
00:07:57,412 --> 00:07:58,915
Why are you looking at me
like that?

139
00:07:58,915 --> 00:08:01,211
Just... what are you doing
here?

140
00:08:01,211 --> 00:08:03,508
I just came back to tie up
a few things.

141
00:08:03,508 --> 00:08:06,221
Wow, must be a pretty big deal if it
brought you all the way back

142
00:08:06,221 --> 00:08:09,019
from New York City to our
humble little town.

143
00:08:09,019 --> 00:08:11,315
It's been... what, 15 years?

144
00:08:12,275 --> 00:08:17,410
Five, actually. I came back to help move
my nan out of the St. Nicholas House

145
00:08:17,410 --> 00:08:19,080
so she could live closer
to me in New York.

146
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:24,508
Right. I heard. I'm... so sorry
I couldn't be there, Ryan.

147
00:08:24,508 --> 00:08:26,804
I loved your grandmother,
I was just...

148
00:08:26,804 --> 00:08:29,267
I was out of state working with
a client and...

149
00:08:29,267 --> 00:08:31,648
It's okay, I heard.

150
00:08:33,108 --> 00:08:34,319
It is really good to see you.

151
00:08:34,319 --> 00:08:38,369
Yeah, it's good to see you
too. You look...

152
00:08:38,369 --> 00:08:40,540
very professional.

153
00:08:41,876 --> 00:08:44,047
- And you look...
- More mature?

154
00:08:44,047 --> 00:08:45,717
Exactly the same.

155
00:08:45,717 --> 00:08:47,470
Oh.

156
00:08:47,470 --> 00:08:51,562
Um... so, are you staying
for Christmas, or...

157
00:08:51,562 --> 00:08:53,525
- I'm considering it.
- Hmm.

158
00:08:53,525 --> 00:08:55,529
We should hang out
if you're free.

159
00:08:55,529 --> 00:08:57,950
Yeah... no... it's actually my busy time
of the year,

160
00:08:57,950 --> 00:09:00,204
so I don't know if we can
work it out, but...

161
00:09:00,204 --> 00:09:01,498
Okay.

162
00:09:01,498 --> 00:09:04,630
You know, my number is still the same,
though, so call me or text me.

163
00:09:04,630 --> 00:09:08,137
Have your people call my people,
we can set something up.

164
00:09:08,137 --> 00:09:09,180
Okay.

165
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:11,184
- Anyway, I should probably run.

166
00:09:11,184 --> 00:09:12,938
I just was trying to get some
inspiration.

167
00:09:12,938 --> 00:09:15,527
Olivia and I are actually in charge
of decorating the tree this year,

168
00:09:15,527 --> 00:09:16,904
but we only have a few days, so...

169
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,704
It's going well, I see.

170
00:09:20,704 --> 00:09:22,457
Stop it, I'm just getting
started.

171
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:26,591
Well, I can't wait to see what
you guys do with it.

172
00:09:26,591 --> 00:09:28,553
Thanks.

173
00:09:30,348 --> 00:09:33,145
So, I guess I'll see you around.

174
00:09:33,145 --> 00:09:36,861
Yeah. Well, it's a small town,
so it's highly likely.

175
00:10:38,651 --> 00:10:40,237
- Hey!
- Hey.

176
00:10:40,237 --> 00:10:43,243
- What are you up to?
- Oh, just procrastinating instead of

177
00:10:43,243 --> 00:10:45,080
designing that Christmas tree.

178
00:10:45,414 --> 00:10:47,920
- Ooh, I had a really good idea.
- Uh-uh?

179
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:50,132
- Woodland creatures.
- Ooh.

180
00:10:50,132 --> 00:10:53,138
Yeah, so we could have like all these
little critters running around the tree.

181
00:10:53,138 --> 00:10:55,685
Wait, you don't mean live
animals, do you?

182
00:10:55,685 --> 00:10:57,606
The idea sounded better in
my head.

183
00:11:00,987 --> 00:11:03,868
Sami! Mayor Hoffman.
Hi.

184
00:11:05,079 --> 00:11:06,289
To what do we owe the pleasure?

185
00:11:06,289 --> 00:11:10,464
Oh, I'm so sorry I can't stay long,
but I have an urgent request

186
00:11:10,464 --> 00:11:11,676
that I wanted to ask in person.

187
00:11:11,676 --> 00:11:14,055
- What's up?
- Do you remember Ribbons and Bows

188
00:11:14,055 --> 00:11:15,976
Fundraiser?
On Christmas Eve.

189
00:11:15,976 --> 00:11:19,148
The one Mrs. St. Nicholas used to host
every year? Yeah, what about it?

190
00:11:19,148 --> 00:11:20,401
We're reviving it.

191
00:11:20,401 --> 00:11:24,910
Well, I'm trying to revive it.
Ryan isn't quite on board yet,

192
00:11:24,910 --> 00:11:27,081
so I was hoping you could talk
to him.

193
00:11:27,874 --> 00:11:29,962
- Uh...
- Ryan? Like...

194
00:11:29,962 --> 00:11:32,759
Ryan St. Nicholas? That Ryan?
- Mm-hmm.

195
00:11:32,759 --> 00:11:35,515
- I think he's in New York.
- He's actually in Ivy Glen right now.

196
00:11:35,515 --> 00:11:37,811
- What?
- I was really hoping you could help me.

197
00:11:37,811 --> 00:11:40,817
Maybe you could talk to him
and see if you can get him on board.

198
00:11:41,276 --> 00:11:44,783
You know what? The Ribbons and Bows
Fundraiser really was his nan's thing,

199
00:11:44,783 --> 00:11:47,496
so if he's not into it, then...

200
00:11:47,496 --> 00:11:51,756
Oh, a lot of people in town could really
use this. It could do a lot of good.

201
00:11:51,756 --> 00:11:53,509
Hmm... and you two are close.

202
00:11:53,509 --> 00:11:55,513
We were close. Then, he went off
to New York

203
00:11:55,513 --> 00:11:58,060
and he created this whole life
I know nothing about.

204
00:11:59,563 --> 00:12:02,109
Well, he would still listen to you.

205
00:12:02,109 --> 00:12:03,863
Could you just try? Please.

206
00:12:05,199 --> 00:12:07,871
I wouldn't ask if it wasn't urgent.
- I don't know.

207
00:12:11,796 --> 00:12:14,425
How about this? I know that this year,

208
00:12:14,425 --> 00:12:17,014
the decorating contract went to Mark
and his team,

209
00:12:17,431 --> 00:12:20,312
as it does every year for
as long as I can remember,

210
00:12:20,312 --> 00:12:23,653
but he's retiring. It's gonna be
up for grabs next year,

211
00:12:23,653 --> 00:12:29,122
so if you can help me get Ryan to host
this year's Ribbons and Bows Fundraiser,

212
00:12:29,122 --> 00:12:34,215
it'll go a long way to seeing that you get
the contract from town council next year.

213
00:12:35,092 --> 00:12:37,848
Okay. How about this?

214
00:12:37,848 --> 00:12:40,352
You will personally guarantee...

215
00:12:40,352 --> 00:12:44,193
Yes, that we will be the top candidate
next year for the contract

216
00:12:44,193 --> 00:12:47,534
if we can get the house
decorated in less than a week?

217
00:12:47,534 --> 00:12:49,328
Sure.

218
00:12:50,623 --> 00:12:52,209
- We'll discuss it.
- We're in.

219
00:12:53,336 --> 00:12:55,592
She's definitely in.
- Okay.

220
00:12:55,592 --> 00:12:58,472
Okay, great. Thank you.

221
00:12:58,472 --> 00:13:01,394
Oh, you two are lifesavers.

222
00:13:01,394 --> 00:13:03,566
- Happy to help.
- Bye, Jack.

223
00:13:03,566 --> 00:13:04,943
Bye, Mayor.

224
00:13:04,943 --> 00:13:08,116
Okay. Umm... wow.

225
00:13:08,116 --> 00:13:11,414
Hmm, looks like you have to get
to St. Nicholas House.

226
00:13:11,414 --> 00:13:17,134
Yeah, looks like I do, uh? I guess I'll
give you guys an update when I get back.

227
00:13:17,134 --> 00:13:19,472
Ryan.

228
00:13:20,307 --> 00:13:22,979
Stop it, Jack!

229
00:13:25,652 --> 00:13:26,862
Huh.

230
00:13:27,781 --> 00:13:29,408
I know that look.

231
00:13:31,747 --> 00:13:33,375
- I have an idea.
- Oh, no.

232
00:13:33,375 --> 00:13:35,212
Not, "Oh, no." Oh, yes!

233
00:13:35,212 --> 00:13:38,594
Whatever operation "Fill In The Blank”
is churning in your mind...

234
00:13:38,594 --> 00:13:40,097
You don't even know what
the idea is.

235
00:13:40,097 --> 00:13:43,563
I know that Grace doesn't need you
meddling in her life.

236
00:13:43,563 --> 00:13:46,025
She's a grown adult,
she's also our business partner.

237
00:13:46,025 --> 00:13:48,029
And she's your sister
and my best friend.

238
00:13:48,029 --> 00:13:49,407
All the more reason not
to meddle.

239
00:13:49,407 --> 00:13:53,123
Okay, Ryan St. Nicholas is back in town,
he's her one that got away.

240
00:13:53,123 --> 00:13:55,210
She has never explicitly
said that.

241
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:56,964
She's had a crush on him since she was
12.

242
00:13:56,964 --> 00:13:59,427
The whole town knows he
feels the same.

243
00:13:59,427 --> 00:14:00,930
They've been friends for years.

244
00:14:00,930 --> 00:14:02,726
If they wanted to date,
they would have by now.

245
00:14:02,726 --> 00:14:05,648
No, they've never had
a chance. Think about it.

246
00:14:05,648 --> 00:14:08,069
Ryan was dating Ryan dated Miranda
in freshman year and then,

247
00:14:08,069 --> 00:14:10,157
when they broke up,
Grace started dating Vince.

248
00:14:10,157 --> 00:14:12,161
- Ugh.
- And then, when they broke up...

249
00:14:12,161 --> 00:14:13,496
Okay, I get it.

250
00:14:13,496 --> 00:14:17,672
But now, they're both single...
I think. Wait.

251
00:14:18,006 --> 00:14:19,216
What are you doing?

252
00:14:19,216 --> 00:14:21,972
I'm just gonna do a quick little social
media stalk,

253
00:14:21,972 --> 00:14:24,603
make sure that he's not in
a relationship.

254
00:14:25,437 --> 00:14:28,778
It doesn't look like he is!

255
00:14:28,778 --> 00:14:30,531
He's single and ready to mingle.

256
00:14:30,531 --> 00:14:34,288
I love you and your little missions,
but it...

257
00:14:34,288 --> 00:14:38,129
now is not the time for another attempt
at operation "Find Grace Love,”

258
00:14:38,129 --> 00:14:40,843
especially not with
Ryan St. Nicholas.

259
00:14:42,012 --> 00:14:46,396
I'm going to order us some dinner.
While I'm gone, don't do any meddling.

260
00:14:49,820 --> 00:14:51,072
No promises.

261
00:15:10,444 --> 00:15:13,951
Well, well, well, look what
the elves dragged in.

262
00:15:13,951 --> 00:15:18,001
Wow! Talk about a glow up.
Lookin' good, Santaman.

263
00:15:18,001 --> 00:15:19,211
- Quinn, how are you, buddy?
- Good.

264
00:15:19,211 --> 00:15:22,426
You know, no one has called me
Santaman since high school.

265
00:15:22,426 --> 00:15:24,305
Ah, it's a waste of a perfectly
good nickname.

266
00:15:24,305 --> 00:15:27,520
I don't know about that.

267
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:29,900
So, what’s this I hear about
you wanting to sell the place?

268
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:30,985
Where did you hear that?

269
00:15:30,985 --> 00:15:33,281
Ah, it's just a rumour around town,

270
00:15:33,281 --> 00:15:36,120
since the place has been empty for what,
like five years, now?

271
00:15:36,120 --> 00:15:40,212
Yeah, no. It was just a quick trip
back to get my nan out of this place.

272
00:15:41,005 --> 00:15:43,384
She didn't want to go, but it was time.

273
00:15:43,384 --> 00:15:46,015
She just couldn't handle this place
anymore, you know?

274
00:15:46,015 --> 00:15:48,311
Oh, man, it's just so weird
being back here without her.

275
00:15:48,311 --> 00:15:51,192
Yeah, losing a loved one is
never easy, man.

276
00:15:51,693 --> 00:15:54,908
Hey, everyone loved your nan.

277
00:15:56,954 --> 00:15:58,582
You know, she actually liked you...

278
00:15:58,582 --> 00:16:02,047
even though you spent half your nights out
in out lawn here with...

279
00:16:02,047 --> 00:16:05,178
putting, what? With the large Christmas
decorations all over our lawn.

280
00:16:05,178 --> 00:16:09,311
- That was all Olivia and you know it.
- Oh, Olivia! Alright, pff.

281
00:16:10,230 --> 00:16:12,401
The house is in pretty good shape.

282
00:16:12,902 --> 00:16:14,698
Yeah, I've had people maintaining it,

283
00:16:14,698 --> 00:16:17,327
making sure everything is in working
order. I just...

284
00:16:17,912 --> 00:16:19,708
I'm not sure what I want to do
with it yet.

285
00:16:19,708 --> 00:16:24,676
Well, if you do decide you want to sell,
I have a very interested buyer,

286
00:16:24,676 --> 00:16:27,222
and if you do sell to me, of course,

287
00:16:27,222 --> 00:16:31,815
I could guarantee you that I would fill
this place with a lot of life.

288
00:16:34,821 --> 00:16:36,199
There you go.

289
00:16:37,911 --> 00:16:40,498
Alright, I'll make you a deal.

290
00:16:40,498 --> 00:16:44,507
If I do decide to sell, I'll call you,
let you make the first offer.

291
00:16:45,008 --> 00:16:46,553
Sounds fair?

292
00:16:46,553 --> 00:16:48,223
Sure.

293
00:16:48,599 --> 00:16:51,145
Sounds good, sounds good.
Go Polar Bears, right?

294
00:16:51,145 --> 00:16:53,149
- Hi.

295
00:16:53,149 --> 00:16:54,527
Hey, Grace.

296
00:16:54,527 --> 00:16:57,241
What's going on here?
You boys behaving yourselves?

297
00:16:57,241 --> 00:16:58,326
Always.

298
00:16:58,326 --> 00:17:01,541
Always? Oh, no. I remember more than one
hockey game where the coach

299
00:17:01,541 --> 00:17:04,421
benched you two for...
what did he call it?

300
00:17:04,421 --> 00:17:06,425
Severe competition.

301
00:17:06,425 --> 00:17:08,012
You know, I thought of it more
as passion.

302
00:17:08,012 --> 00:17:11,394
Passion, yeah, that's it.
Passion's the word you're looking for.

303
00:17:11,394 --> 00:17:13,524
Alright, I'll get out of your hair.

304
00:17:13,524 --> 00:17:16,780
Uh... I'm gonna grab a bite at
Beth’s Bistro, if you're free.

305
00:17:17,197 --> 00:17:21,999
Oh, I... I... I have some work
I gotta get done, so...

306
00:17:22,499 --> 00:17:24,169
Okay.

307
00:17:24,169 --> 00:17:27,134
But if my schedule changes,
I'll text you later.

308
00:17:27,134 --> 00:17:29,221
Sounds good.

309
00:17:33,689 --> 00:17:36,528
- You and Quinn, uh? Oh, okay.
- It's complicated.

310
00:17:36,528 --> 00:17:40,201
- Yeah? Oh.
- We're just... hanging out sometimes...

311
00:17:40,201 --> 00:17:42,456
whenever we're both free.

312
00:17:42,456 --> 00:17:45,838
It's nothing serious, we're just the last
two single people left in Ivy Glen.

313
00:17:46,631 --> 00:17:48,719
Anyway, I...

314
00:17:48,719 --> 00:17:50,347
Came here to talk to you about

315
00:17:50,347 --> 00:17:52,184
the Ribbons and Bows Fundraiser.

316
00:17:52,184 --> 00:17:53,896
- You did?
- Mm-hmm.

317
00:17:53,896 --> 00:17:56,526
- Let me guess, Sami sent you.
- Oh, she did. She was very insistent.

318
00:17:56,526 --> 00:17:59,281
Hmm, it's good to see that Sami will
still do whatever she can

319
00:17:59,281 --> 00:18:01,160
to get what she believes in.

320
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,538
Yeah, but she has a point.

321
00:18:02,538 --> 00:18:05,251
I mean, come on, your nan's fundraiser,
it did a lot of good

322
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:07,130
for Ivy Glen back in the day and...

323
00:18:08,091 --> 00:18:11,723
you know, with the way things are,
it could a lot of people

324
00:18:11,723 --> 00:18:13,309
if you brought it back.

325
00:18:13,686 --> 00:18:15,898
Listen, I know that's the last thing you
probably want to hear,

326
00:18:15,898 --> 00:18:18,862
but I'll help you, okay?
Anything you need, just consider it done.

327
00:18:18,862 --> 00:18:22,244
I've already made a list of vendors that
I think would work for the place and...

328
00:18:22,244 --> 00:18:25,835
it would really mean a lot to me
for this opportunity, I just...

329
00:18:27,087 --> 00:18:28,715
I love it here.

330
00:18:29,466 --> 00:18:31,429
So?

331
00:18:31,429 --> 00:18:35,270
What do you say? Will you let me help you
revive the Ribbons and Bows Fundraiser?

332
00:18:38,317 --> 00:18:40,155
Please.

333
00:18:40,739 --> 00:18:42,159
I'll make it really easy for you, okay?

334
00:18:42,159 --> 00:18:44,246
Olivia and Jack and I,
we will handle everything.

335
00:18:44,246 --> 00:18:46,835
All you have to do is open up the place
and we will take care of the rest...

336
00:18:46,835 --> 00:18:48,964
Okay, okay, okay.
So, you'll do absolutely everything?

337
00:18:48,964 --> 00:18:51,970
All you have to do is smile and wave,
and you're good at that.

338
00:18:54,308 --> 00:18:56,897
- Okay, you know what? Fine.

339
00:18:56,897 --> 00:18:58,567
Let's do it.
- Okay, great! Yes!

340
00:18:58,567 --> 00:19:00,445
- It could be fun.
- It'll be so much fun!

341
00:19:00,445 --> 00:19:02,909
Okay, so do you want to meet tomorrow
morning at the café,

342
00:19:02,909 --> 00:19:03,952
we could start planning?

343
00:19:03,952 --> 00:19:06,583
- Yeah, let's do that.
- Okay, sounds good.

344
00:19:21,988 --> 00:19:25,788
- Okay, so tomorrow at the café?
- Yeah.

345
00:19:25,788 --> 00:19:28,292
- With Ryan St. Nicholas?
- Yeah.

346
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:31,382
Oh, wow, okay. I'm just gonna
go run an errand.

347
00:19:31,382 --> 00:19:33,302
- Do you want me to go with you?

348
00:19:33,302 --> 00:19:36,100
No, it's okay sweetie, I'll be quick.
I'll see you at home.

349
00:19:39,398 --> 00:19:42,530
- You good?
- Yeah, great. Why?

350
00:19:42,863 --> 00:19:46,453
Just, you know, Ryan.

351
00:19:46,453 --> 00:19:50,754
Come on! He was my high school
crush, Jack, okay? I am so over it.

352
00:19:50,754 --> 00:19:54,846
- I just know he was...
- A great friend, nothing more...

353
00:19:54,846 --> 00:19:57,267
which is great. I love great
friends, they're... great.

354
00:19:57,267 --> 00:19:58,311
Great?

355
00:19:58,311 --> 00:19:59,522
- Stop it.

356
00:19:59,522 --> 00:20:02,319
I'm just trying to be a good
big brother and look out for you.

357
00:20:02,319 --> 00:20:06,786
Okay, you're a great big brother and
I love you, but I'm a big girl, okay?

358
00:20:06,786 --> 00:20:11,546
The charm of Ryan St. Nicholas
has long since passed.

359
00:20:11,546 --> 00:20:12,840
Okay.

360
00:20:14,259 --> 00:20:17,683
Listen, I'm gonna order dinner.
Do you want sweet and sour chicken?

361
00:20:17,683 --> 00:20:18,935
Does that sound good?
- Mm-hmm.

362
00:20:18,935 --> 00:20:20,606
Egg rolls.
- Obviously.

363
00:20:20,606 --> 00:20:22,400
Yeah.

364
00:22:24,352 --> 00:22:26,649
What's wrong?
- Nothing.

365
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:29,697
- Hey, good timing.
- Hello.

366
00:22:30,281 --> 00:22:33,997
Wow. I've had so many
post-game milkshakes here.

367
00:22:33,997 --> 00:22:35,834
- Oh, yeah.
- Everything is the same.

368
00:22:35,834 --> 00:22:36,961
Yeah.

369
00:22:36,961 --> 00:22:38,798
It's kind of nice how things
don't change.

370
00:22:38,798 --> 00:22:40,802
Yeah, it is.

371
00:22:40,802 --> 00:22:42,890
Alright, let's grab a table.

372
00:22:48,818 --> 00:22:49,946
Thank you.

373
00:22:49,946 --> 00:22:53,285
The key to a great design is a strong
theme and since this is your fundraiser,

374
00:22:53,285 --> 00:22:54,914
I would love to get your thoughts.

375
00:22:54,914 --> 00:22:58,212
- Oh, sorry. That's one of our clients.

376
00:22:58,212 --> 00:23:00,884
I gotta take this.
I will be right back.

377
00:23:01,468 --> 00:23:03,723
Hi, Sarah.
Yeah, it's a good time.

378
00:23:06,395 --> 00:23:08,733
You guys seem pretty busy.
You sure you got time for this?

379
00:23:08,733 --> 00:23:12,156
Yeah, we got this. Come on, I know your
nan's house as well as I know my own.

380
00:23:12,156 --> 00:23:14,745
I mean, I haven't been back to the
St. Nicholas House in a few years, but...

381
00:23:14,745 --> 00:23:16,123
Nothing's changed.

382
00:23:16,123 --> 00:23:17,876
Must be hard, going back there
without her.

383
00:23:17,876 --> 00:23:19,379
Yeah. No, it is.

384
00:23:19,379 --> 00:23:21,634
It's gonna be hard having
Christmas without her.

385
00:23:21,634 --> 00:23:23,763
Yeah, but you know what?
She would be so proud

386
00:23:23,763 --> 00:23:25,892
that you're reviving the Ribbons
and Bows Fundraiser,

387
00:23:25,892 --> 00:23:27,353
that always meant a lot to her.

388
00:23:27,353 --> 00:23:30,902
I was hesitant to do it, but honestly,
feels like the right thing to do.

389
00:23:30,902 --> 00:23:32,030
Hmm.

390
00:23:32,030 --> 00:23:34,577
Will your parents be joining?
They were always the life of the party.

391
00:23:34,577 --> 00:23:35,996
- No, not this year.

392
00:23:35,996 --> 00:23:38,208
They're actually backpacking
through Europe right now.

393
00:23:38,208 --> 00:23:39,419
That's awesome.

394
00:23:39,419 --> 00:23:41,089
I know! I'm so happy they're finally
doing it.

395
00:23:41,089 --> 00:23:43,595
It was always on my bucket list to go
backpacking through Europe.

396
00:23:43,595 --> 00:23:45,974
Yeah, mine too.

397
00:23:47,101 --> 00:23:48,730
We should make that happen, then.

398
00:23:50,609 --> 00:23:52,905
Um... so, this design.

399
00:23:52,905 --> 00:23:55,451
Okay, how about this?
Come over to the house.

400
00:23:55,451 --> 00:23:58,583
We'll go room to room,
see if we spark an inspiration.

401
00:23:58,583 --> 00:24:00,587
That'd be great.

402
00:24:01,338 --> 00:24:03,133
- You gonna get that?

403
00:24:03,133 --> 00:24:07,851
Oh... that's just Quinn. You want
to get some hot chocolates to go?

404
00:24:08,937 --> 00:24:10,189
- Yeah.
- Great.

405
00:24:10,189 --> 00:24:11,274
Okay.

406
00:24:13,988 --> 00:24:16,493
Can we get two hot chocolates
to go, please? Thanks.

407
00:24:17,871 --> 00:24:21,671
- This your work?
- Yeah. Yeah, it is. What do you think?

408
00:24:21,671 --> 00:24:23,382
Meh.

409
00:24:23,382 --> 00:24:25,762
Kidding. The decorations look amazing.

410
00:24:25,762 --> 00:24:28,392
Thanks. And it's really too bad that
we didn't get the contract

411
00:24:28,392 --> 00:24:30,522
to decorate Ivy Glen's downtown
this year.

412
00:24:30,522 --> 00:24:31,732
Yeah, but we will next year.

413
00:24:31,732 --> 00:24:32,776
Thanks.

414
00:24:32,776 --> 00:24:35,740
Hey. I'm gonna head back.
Jack's waiting on me to wrap the gifts

415
00:24:35,740 --> 00:24:37,619
for the children that we're sponsoring
this year.

416
00:24:37,619 --> 00:24:40,166
I'm about two hours late.
I'll see you both soon.

417
00:24:40,166 --> 00:24:42,044
- See you soon.
- Bye.

418
00:24:42,504 --> 00:24:46,596
So, is it weird being back?
I mean, so much has changed.

419
00:24:48,015 --> 00:24:49,184
What do you mean?

420
00:24:49,184 --> 00:24:51,229
Come on, everything about you
is different.

421
00:24:51,229 --> 00:24:55,404
You left this town as a boy in a scraggly
white t-shirt with jeans

422
00:24:55,404 --> 00:24:57,283
and you came back as a...

423
00:24:57,283 --> 00:25:00,957
as a business tycoon in a very,
very posh suit.

424
00:25:00,957 --> 00:25:03,462
- It is bespoke, thank you for noticing.
- Hmm.

425
00:25:04,965 --> 00:25:06,886
Tell me about your business.

426
00:25:06,886 --> 00:25:10,685
Oh, well, we are a full-scale decorating
and design firm

427
00:25:10,685 --> 00:25:14,860
and we do everything from house
remodels all the way

428
00:25:14,860 --> 00:25:17,574
to holiday decorating depending
on the client's needs.

429
00:25:17,574 --> 00:25:18,952
So, what made you get into that?

430
00:25:18,952 --> 00:25:22,166
Uh, my first year in college,
I took a decorating course

431
00:25:22,166 --> 00:25:27,260
and it was just a throwaway course,
but it changed everything, changed me.

432
00:25:27,928 --> 00:25:30,600
I don't know, I always thought you were
gonna do something with fashion.

433
00:25:30,600 --> 00:25:32,688
- Fashion? Why?

434
00:25:32,688 --> 00:25:35,025
You're just so bold, you know?

435
00:25:35,025 --> 00:25:37,113
Do you remember when I bet you
you couldn't wear

436
00:25:37,113 --> 00:25:38,908
my nan's Mrs. Claus outfit
for an entire week?

437
00:25:38,908 --> 00:25:41,789
- I did.
- Oh, you did. You showed up every day

438
00:25:41,789 --> 00:25:45,421
with a wig, the glasses,
that big fluffy dress...

439
00:25:45,922 --> 00:25:47,551
I'm not gonna lie,
I was pretty impressed.

440
00:25:47,551 --> 00:25:50,055
Yeah. Well, mister Bentford
wasn't very impressed.

441
00:25:50,055 --> 00:25:52,894
He called me out in front of the entire
chemistry class, remember that?

442
00:25:52,894 --> 00:25:55,232
Yeah. Well, he never had
a sense of humour anyway.

443
00:25:55,232 --> 00:25:56,527
No, he didn't.

444
00:25:56,527 --> 00:25:58,113
Thank you.

445
00:25:58,113 --> 00:26:00,242
There you go. Thank you.
Keep the change.

446
00:26:03,248 --> 00:26:04,960
You always knew how to make
everyone laugh.

447
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:06,505
Oh, I don't know about that.

448
00:26:06,505 --> 00:26:08,425
Well, for me, at least.

449
00:26:08,425 --> 00:26:10,722
Since that first day when
I was the new kid in Ivy Glen.

450
00:26:10,722 --> 00:26:13,393
You know, I took my duties
as the unofficial head of the high school

451
00:26:13,393 --> 00:26:15,439
welcoming committee very seriously.

452
00:26:15,439 --> 00:26:18,613
Well, you made that transition
to live with my nan much easier.

453
00:26:18,613 --> 00:26:20,115
I'm glad I could help.

454
00:26:20,115 --> 00:26:23,205
Oh, speaking of help, if you need me to
do anything for the fundraiser,

455
00:26:23,205 --> 00:26:25,417
I know you said that you would
take care of everything,

456
00:26:26,127 --> 00:26:29,676
but if you need help, I'm here,
because that's what friends are for.

457
00:26:29,676 --> 00:26:31,221
Yeah.

458
00:26:31,597 --> 00:26:32,974
We're still friends, though, right?

459
00:26:32,974 --> 00:26:35,939
Oh, come on, of course, we're friends.
We're always gonna be friends.

460
00:26:35,939 --> 00:26:37,567
Listen, I should get going.

461
00:26:37,567 --> 00:26:39,530
Okay. Text me if you want
to come by the house.

462
00:26:39,530 --> 00:26:41,659
Okay.

463
00:26:41,659 --> 00:26:42,786
Grace.

464
00:26:42,786 --> 00:26:44,748
Yeah?

465
00:26:44,748 --> 00:26:46,418
Really good to see you.

466
00:26:46,418 --> 00:26:49,633
Good to see you too,
Ryan St. Nicholas.

467
00:26:54,058 --> 00:26:57,314
I'm telling you,
this is the move!

468
00:26:57,314 --> 00:26:59,360
- No, no.
- Yes, yes, yes!

469
00:26:59,360 --> 00:27:01,866
This could finally be their perfect
moment.

470
00:27:01,866 --> 00:27:04,120
Timing is everything, right?

471
00:27:04,120 --> 00:27:09,213
Plus, Grace deserves her own love story.
This is just a little nudge.

472
00:27:09,213 --> 00:27:11,134
Olivia, please, stop.

473
00:27:11,134 --> 00:27:15,852
You didn't see her.
It affected her, it was so cute.

474
00:27:16,687 --> 00:27:19,943
Like... okay. Do you remember
the Christmas pageant

475
00:27:19,943 --> 00:27:21,947
that your mom talked
us into doing?

476
00:27:22,532 --> 00:27:24,995
The one where Grace and Ryan
thought they were gonna be

477
00:27:24,995 --> 00:27:28,043
background understudies, but then,
got wrangled into playing Mary and Joseph?

478
00:27:28,043 --> 00:27:33,345
Yes, yes, and do you remember how they
were so locked into one another?

479
00:27:33,345 --> 00:27:36,351
Like no one else mattered,
it was just the two of them?

480
00:27:36,351 --> 00:27:38,230
Olivia, they were ten-years-old.

481
00:27:38,230 --> 00:27:40,610
I think they were more focused
on not forgetting their lines

482
00:27:40,610 --> 00:27:42,864
and embarrassing themselves
in front of the whole town.

483
00:27:42,864 --> 00:27:46,454
Okay, maybe, but you didn't
see them at the café.

484
00:27:46,454 --> 00:27:48,793
The way that she was looking
at him,

485
00:27:48,793 --> 00:27:52,091
I have never seen her look
at anyone like that before.

486
00:27:53,134 --> 00:27:57,727
They are so perfect for each other,
the timing just never been right...

487
00:27:58,270 --> 00:27:59,523
until now.

488
00:28:00,190 --> 00:28:01,150
What?

489
00:28:01,150 --> 00:28:03,071
I have a plan.

490
00:28:03,071 --> 00:28:05,075
- You're kidding me.

491
00:28:05,535 --> 00:28:07,121
Mistletoe.

492
00:28:07,706 --> 00:28:11,462
- Isn't mistletoe Grace's thing?
- It's mine, now.

493
00:28:12,172 --> 00:28:17,892
Operation Mistletoe. I am getting them
under this if it is the last thing I do.

494
00:28:18,894 --> 00:28:20,230
Why?

495
00:28:20,230 --> 00:28:24,447
Because, she's my best friend,
and even if she can't see it right now,

496
00:28:25,198 --> 00:28:26,952
this is the right thing for her.

497
00:28:26,952 --> 00:28:29,415
They've never been single
at the same time.

498
00:28:29,415 --> 00:28:33,883
Okay, step one, the café, check.

499
00:28:33,883 --> 00:28:35,427
- You didn't?
- I did, yeah,

500
00:28:35,427 --> 00:28:37,682
but we didn't end up
sitting at the right table.

501
00:28:37,682 --> 00:28:41,649
Umm, but step two, I'm gonna put
it at St. Nicholas House,

502
00:28:42,024 --> 00:28:45,447
and step three, I'm just gonna put
them all over Ivy Glen.

503
00:28:45,447 --> 00:28:47,786
I mean, nothing says romance

504
00:28:47,786 --> 00:28:49,748
like the magic of mistletoe!

505
00:28:50,457 --> 00:28:52,921
You know what? You're right.

506
00:28:54,423 --> 00:28:56,260
Nothing does.

507
00:29:02,816 --> 00:29:08,368
Okay, I got one for the office,
two for St. Nicholas house,

508
00:29:08,368 --> 00:29:10,998
I did one for the café.

509
00:29:11,542 --> 00:29:14,088
- Hey. What 'cha doing?
- Oh! Uh...

510
00:29:14,088 --> 00:29:16,342
just looking for my
lip gloss and I found it.

511
00:29:16,342 --> 00:29:18,263
- Do you want some hot chocolate?
- Yeah, sure.

512
00:29:18,263 --> 00:29:20,518
Um, two hot chocolates, please.

513
00:29:20,893 --> 00:29:23,273
- Hey, Grace, Olivia.
- Quinn, hi.

514
00:29:23,273 --> 00:29:26,362
I'm glad I caught you. I just wanted to
swing by on my way to work

515
00:29:26,362 --> 00:29:28,241
to run something by you.
- What's up?

516
00:29:28,241 --> 00:29:31,497
Okay, I'm working with a major investor,
a luxury condo group

517
00:29:31,497 --> 00:29:34,044
looking to expand into our little town,
how cool is that?

518
00:29:34,044 --> 00:29:37,009
Cool or madly destructive
to our town's integrity?

519
00:29:37,009 --> 00:29:39,723
Olivia. She's just kidding,
Quinn.

520
00:29:39,723 --> 00:29:41,309
She's always been a kidder, huh?

521
00:29:41,309 --> 00:29:46,319
Anyways, I just have to find them
the perfect location and we're good to go,

522
00:29:46,319 --> 00:29:49,200
but I would love for you to
design the space.

523
00:29:49,200 --> 00:29:50,410
Sounds amazing.

524
00:29:50,410 --> 00:29:53,416
It would be huge and it could
put Keene and Rankin on the map,

525
00:29:53,416 --> 00:29:57,007
and it would boost local business.
Mayor Hoffman agrees.

526
00:29:57,007 --> 00:29:59,679
Yeah, we... we love that idea.
That sounds great,

527
00:29:59,679 --> 00:30:01,683
we can't wait to hear more, can we,
Olivia?

528
00:30:01,683 --> 00:30:03,353
- Yeah.
- Okay. Um... oh,

529
00:30:03,353 --> 00:30:05,733
did you want a hot chocolate, Quinn?

530
00:30:05,733 --> 00:30:08,404
Uh, ye... no, no,
I'm good, but talk soon?

531
00:30:08,404 --> 00:30:09,991
- Sure.
- Okay.

532
00:30:09,991 --> 00:30:12,705
- Oh, sorry. Okay.

533
00:30:14,626 --> 00:30:18,466
Wow. I have seen rocks have more
chemistry than you two.

534
00:30:18,466 --> 00:30:21,890
At lest, he's nice and he's smart and
you know, successful.

535
00:30:21,890 --> 00:30:24,646
That's... that checks some boxes.

536
00:30:24,646 --> 00:30:27,527
Well, that's love is,
it's just a box to be checked.

537
00:30:27,527 --> 00:30:29,990
Okay. Listen, I'll see you in a few
hours to get started on the tree.

538
00:30:29,990 --> 00:30:31,033
In a few hours?

539
00:30:31,033 --> 00:30:32,912
Yeah, I told Ryan I'd stop by
the St. Nicholas House

540
00:30:32,912 --> 00:30:34,833
so that we can talk about the design.
You know what?

541
00:30:34,833 --> 00:30:36,377
I should get him a coffee too.

542
00:30:36,670 --> 00:30:39,509
Ah, well, maybe while you're there,
you could go on the porch,

543
00:30:39,509 --> 00:30:43,182
like, really take it all in,
maybe he's there with you.

544
00:30:43,893 --> 00:30:45,980
Okay, I know you, Olivia,
what are you up to?

545
00:30:45,980 --> 00:30:48,944
I... just taking care of our
most important client.

546
00:30:48,944 --> 00:30:51,783
You have a glint in your eye,
got something up your sleeve?

547
00:30:51,783 --> 00:30:54,496
Santa’s elves never reveal
their secrets.

548
00:30:54,496 --> 00:30:56,500
Okay.

549
00:30:56,500 --> 00:30:58,631
I gotta find some fancy
coffee shop.

550
00:31:11,405 --> 00:31:14,829
Hey, right on time. What...
what's this?

551
00:31:14,829 --> 00:31:17,376
A flat white with oat milk
and two sugars

552
00:31:18,837 --> 00:31:20,090
How did you know my coffee
order?

553
00:31:20,090 --> 00:31:21,927
Oh, come on, isn't that
the typical big city order?

554
00:31:21,927 --> 00:31:24,139
Oh, okay. Well, what's your order?

555
00:31:24,139 --> 00:31:26,060
Just in case, you know, I want to return
the favour.

556
00:31:26,060 --> 00:31:28,106
Oh, just a small drip coffee
with two creamers.

557
00:31:28,106 --> 00:31:31,320
- Simple and classic, I like it.
- Yeah.

558
00:31:31,780 --> 00:31:33,617
Oh...

559
00:31:34,869 --> 00:31:38,459
- I did not know that was there.
- Yeah, me neither. Um...

560
00:31:39,963 --> 00:31:42,885
- I mean, we shouldn't, right?
- What? No. Ew.

561
00:31:42,885 --> 00:31:44,138
Ew?

562
00:31:44,138 --> 00:31:47,687
I don't mean like ew, ew,
I just mean...

563
00:31:47,687 --> 00:31:49,649
...why? Did you want to kiss me?

564
00:31:49,649 --> 00:31:50,985
No.

565
00:31:51,862 --> 00:31:53,782
Did you want to kiss me?
- No.

566
00:31:53,782 --> 00:31:56,955
- Okay, then we're good.
- Yeah, totally, totally good.

567
00:31:57,999 --> 00:32:01,005
We should probably just take that down,
though. It's a little dangerous.

568
00:32:01,005 --> 00:32:03,552
- I got it, I got it.
- Hanging up there like that, you know?

569
00:32:03,927 --> 00:32:05,681
- Let's put that right in your purse.
- Great.

570
00:32:05,681 --> 00:32:07,434
- Anyway, it's cold,

571
00:32:07,434 --> 00:32:09,354
so maybe we should just get inside.

572
00:32:09,354 --> 00:32:12,235
- Yeah, okay.
- Alright, let's get started.

573
00:32:12,737 --> 00:32:15,158
Thank you.
- No problem.

574
00:32:16,578 --> 00:32:18,540
Wow!

575
00:32:18,540 --> 00:32:20,418
This is in a lot better shape
than I was expecting,

576
00:32:20,418 --> 00:32:22,422
already done some decorating
too, nice job.

577
00:32:22,422 --> 00:32:24,176
Oh, no, these were my nan's decorations,

578
00:32:24,176 --> 00:32:26,305
we just didn't take them down
after she left.

579
00:32:26,305 --> 00:32:27,975
She always had great taste.

580
00:32:28,685 --> 00:32:32,442
Hum! The smell of this place brings me
right back to high school.

581
00:32:32,442 --> 00:32:34,071
I know. I'd always make
the cleaning crew

582
00:32:34,071 --> 00:32:36,618
use the exact same pine stuff
that my nan would.

583
00:32:36,618 --> 00:32:39,164
Oh. It's nice that some things
stay the same.

584
00:32:39,164 --> 00:32:41,711
Well, I'm starting to realize
that you're not the same at all.

585
00:32:41,711 --> 00:32:43,590
- I'm not?
- No, you're more...

586
00:32:43,590 --> 00:32:47,097
Hilarious? Good-looking?
Wildly well spoken?

587
00:32:48,851 --> 00:32:53,025
You're more yourself. It's cool to see
you like this, focused, in your element.

588
00:32:53,025 --> 00:32:55,698
It's really nice of you to say.

589
00:32:55,698 --> 00:32:57,033
Well, I meant it.

590
00:32:58,161 --> 00:33:02,503
Mm! You know, that was always
my favourite of your nan's decorations.

591
00:33:02,503 --> 00:33:04,131
- This one?
- Yeah!

592
00:33:04,131 --> 00:33:05,926
This is my eighth grade
masterpiece.

593
00:33:05,926 --> 00:33:08,389
Eighth grade?
You made that in eighth grade?

594
00:33:08,389 --> 00:33:11,103
Hold on, are you... mocking my
art skills?

595
00:33:11,103 --> 00:33:14,109
No, I would never.
I'm being serious, I love it.

596
00:33:14,109 --> 00:33:15,821
I mean, she has a lot of great
decorations,

597
00:33:15,821 --> 00:33:17,199
but that one, that's the best.

598
00:33:17,199 --> 00:33:21,248
Man. So why did you leave it up
after all these years?

599
00:33:22,793 --> 00:33:24,631
I just didn't have the heart
to take it down.

600
00:33:25,089 --> 00:33:27,887
I hired a caregiver for my nan
after grad school

601
00:33:27,887 --> 00:33:31,185
and I realized I wouldn't be able to make
it out here as frequently as I wanted to.

602
00:33:31,937 --> 00:33:33,481
I should have visited more.

603
00:33:33,481 --> 00:33:35,318
The last few months here,
the caregiver said

604
00:33:35,318 --> 00:33:37,823
that she thought every morning
was Christmas.

605
00:33:38,449 --> 00:33:40,161
I just couldn't take that away
from her.

606
00:33:40,161 --> 00:33:42,332
I'm glad you didn't.

607
00:33:42,792 --> 00:33:46,048
I even went and decorated her room at
the care facility by my place.

608
00:33:46,675 --> 00:33:49,179
Stayed up for five years until
she passed.

609
00:33:50,098 --> 00:33:53,939
Well, there's nothing like the Christmas
spirit to get through hard times.

610
00:33:55,985 --> 00:34:00,326
You know, what do you think
about adding to her collection?

611
00:34:01,120 --> 00:34:02,289
What do you mean?

612
00:34:02,289 --> 00:34:05,879
I mean, we don't have a theme yet
and this is really beautiful.

613
00:34:05,879 --> 00:34:08,217
I mean, of course, we'd have to add more
and update a bit,

614
00:34:08,217 --> 00:34:12,058
but I think it's a really good starting
point... if you'd like.

615
00:34:13,102 --> 00:34:15,106
- I would like that.
- Great.

616
00:34:15,566 --> 00:34:17,068
Glad to know we're on
the same page.

617
00:34:17,068 --> 00:34:21,911
I mean, we still need to get a cohesive
theme to bring it all together, but yeah.

618
00:34:22,329 --> 00:34:24,082
Okay, which room is next?

619
00:34:24,082 --> 00:34:26,170
Right here.

620
00:34:31,263 --> 00:34:33,769
So, you and Quinn, I know you
said it wasn't anything serious.

621
00:34:33,769 --> 00:34:36,190
- Look, it's really not, okay?

622
00:34:36,190 --> 00:34:37,526
We're good friends, you know?

623
00:34:37,526 --> 00:34:39,572
It's nice to have somebody to go
to the movies with.

624
00:34:39,572 --> 00:34:42,828
- Okay, so hypothetically...
- Mm-hmm?

625
00:34:42,828 --> 00:34:45,375
If someone were to ask
you out...

626
00:34:45,375 --> 00:34:47,003
Well, I would have to evaluate,
you know?

627
00:34:47,003 --> 00:34:48,715
See if it fits to my work schedule.

628
00:34:48,715 --> 00:34:51,387
Okay. Makes sense.

629
00:34:51,763 --> 00:34:54,476
How about you? I'm sure a lot
of ladies love a bespoke suit.

630
00:34:54,476 --> 00:34:56,689
- Some of them do.

631
00:34:56,689 --> 00:34:58,109
Okay.

632
00:34:58,109 --> 00:35:00,363
- I am kind of in the same boat.
- Yeah?

633
00:35:00,363 --> 00:35:03,202
Everything at the firm is just
going so well that...

634
00:35:04,037 --> 00:35:06,500
I don't know, I just haven't given
any thought to dating.

635
00:35:06,500 --> 00:35:10,383
Oh. Well, you know, I am just so
relieved to know that we both grew up

636
00:35:10,383 --> 00:35:12,303
to be adults with a great
work-life balance.

637
00:35:14,517 --> 00:35:17,188
Ugh. I mean, my last
relationship was...

638
00:35:17,565 --> 00:35:20,236
gosh, five years ago, maybe?
- Oof, what happened?

639
00:35:20,236 --> 00:35:23,117
He was a really great guy,
he was in sales and...

640
00:35:23,117 --> 00:35:26,248
I mean, he was really nice,
but we just...

641
00:35:26,749 --> 00:35:30,549
ugh, you know, we didn't have that
thing, you know? That spark.

642
00:35:31,216 --> 00:35:35,099
And I think we both knew it, but we were
just so good on paper

643
00:35:35,099 --> 00:35:37,395
and we were trying to
make it work, but...

644
00:35:37,730 --> 00:35:40,777
I realized that wasn't what was
best for both of us.

645
00:35:41,445 --> 00:35:44,493
- No one else since?
- Oh, couple dates here and there.

646
00:35:44,493 --> 00:35:47,625
- Yeah, Quinn, right?
- Okay, but chemistry is hard to fake.

647
00:35:47,625 --> 00:35:51,423
Oh, you tell me. These days, it's like
finding lightning in a bottle.

648
00:35:51,841 --> 00:35:54,764
You know, it's funny, I feel like I'm at
that age

649
00:35:54,764 --> 00:35:56,976
where I can finally come up
for air.

650
00:35:56,976 --> 00:36:01,528
For years, I just had my nose to
the grindstone, working late,

651
00:36:01,528 --> 00:36:04,700
just doing whatever it takes to get
the job done,

652
00:36:04,700 --> 00:36:06,245
not giving it a second thought.

653
00:36:06,788 --> 00:36:09,710
- And now?
- Now?

654
00:36:10,127 --> 00:36:15,597
I don't know, I just... kind of feel like
there's a shift in my life.

655
00:36:16,139 --> 00:36:18,895
Everything that's happened in this
last year with my nan passing,

656
00:36:18,895 --> 00:36:22,945
with realizing how much time
and dedication I put into work,

657
00:36:22,945 --> 00:36:25,408
time that I'll never get back.

658
00:36:25,826 --> 00:36:29,291
I mean, it's like someone turned on
the lights and I could see everything

659
00:36:29,291 --> 00:36:32,171
that I gave up to get what I have.

660
00:36:32,171 --> 00:36:34,635
There's still time.

661
00:36:34,635 --> 00:36:37,348
- Not with my nan.

662
00:36:37,683 --> 00:36:41,608
I mean, yes, I moved her as close to me as
possible so I could spend as much time

663
00:36:41,608 --> 00:36:43,820
with her as I could, but...

664
00:36:44,154 --> 00:36:46,116
it's never enough, you know?

665
00:36:47,285 --> 00:36:51,209
I mean, she was the only family
that I had and now...

666
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:54,424
And now, you can start your
own family from the ground up.

667
00:36:56,303 --> 00:36:57,932
If you want to.

668
00:37:01,522 --> 00:37:05,154
- Should... we go see the sun porch?

669
00:37:05,154 --> 00:37:07,325
Yeah, sure.

670
00:37:10,122 --> 00:37:12,126
Do you remember sophomore year
when my nan hosted

671
00:37:12,126 --> 00:37:13,546
that huge Christmas dinner?

672
00:37:13,546 --> 00:37:15,132
Oh, come on, are you kidding?

673
00:37:15,132 --> 00:37:17,470
The first time I had Christmas
Goose was in this very house.

674
00:37:17,470 --> 00:37:19,307
Yeah? You had it since?

675
00:37:19,307 --> 00:37:21,813
Oh, come on, nobody in this
town makes Christmas Goose.

676
00:37:21,813 --> 00:37:26,279
Oh, and her hot chestnut stuffing,
I still dream about it to this day.

677
00:37:26,279 --> 00:37:31,833
I know. I... I tried to make it last
year when my nan left me her recipe and...

678
00:37:32,668 --> 00:37:36,634
yeah, it was a massive fail.
I burnt everything.

679
00:37:36,634 --> 00:37:39,097
Well, maybe we could recreate
it some time.

680
00:37:39,097 --> 00:37:41,393
I happen to be surprisingly
a very good cook.

681
00:37:41,393 --> 00:37:46,529
Well, if your baking is any indication
of your cooking, I can't wait to try.

682
00:37:47,614 --> 00:37:51,079
Oh, it's like stepping back in time,
I just love it.

683
00:37:51,079 --> 00:37:53,459
Oh, yes. Okay, strike a pose.

684
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:57,801
You haven't aged a bit.

685
00:37:57,801 --> 00:38:00,222
Do you remember your Christmas
cookies you used to make?

686
00:38:00,222 --> 00:38:01,851
My nan used to love those.

687
00:38:01,851 --> 00:38:04,105
She said it reminded her
of her childhood.

688
00:38:04,607 --> 00:38:07,821
I tried to recreate them and it
just wasn't the same.

689
00:38:07,821 --> 00:38:09,742
Are you talking about my
Christmas sugar cookies?

690
00:38:10,744 --> 00:38:11,829
I had no idea.

691
00:38:11,829 --> 00:38:14,334
Yeah. Well, if I didn't tell you,
I meant to.

692
00:38:14,752 --> 00:38:16,923
Well, then, I'll have to make you
a batch while you're in town.

693
00:38:16,923 --> 00:38:18,968
Please.

694
00:38:21,599 --> 00:38:22,935
Have dinner with me.

695
00:38:22,935 --> 00:38:26,149
Come on, Ryan, it's like
11 o'clock in the morning.

696
00:38:26,149 --> 00:38:29,072
- I know, I meant later.
- Oh.

697
00:38:29,072 --> 00:38:30,449
You know, I would love to,

698
00:38:30,449 --> 00:38:32,663
but I have to decorate that Christmas
tree tonight.

699
00:38:32,663 --> 00:38:34,374
- Yeah, I forgot.
- Yeah.

700
00:38:34,374 --> 00:38:36,336
Okay, what about another time?

701
00:38:36,671 --> 00:38:39,050
As friends, just friends,
old friends.

702
00:38:39,635 --> 00:38:42,724
Yeah, maybe. Um... let me
check my schedule.

703
00:38:42,724 --> 00:38:44,770
Oh, I forgot your busy schedule.

704
00:38:44,770 --> 00:38:47,776
Let me just check, okay? Please.

705
00:38:49,153 --> 00:38:52,160
So, Town Square, do you know
what you're doing yet?

706
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:53,872
Yeah, I do.

707
00:38:53,872 --> 00:38:55,917
I'll tell you, but you gotta keep it
a secret.

708
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:57,754
I like things to be a surprise.

709
00:38:58,338 --> 00:39:00,092
- Lips are sealed.
- Alright.

710
00:39:00,092 --> 00:39:02,305
And I'll even show you some
of my designs.

711
00:39:02,305 --> 00:39:07,774
So, I was thinking that I wanted
to tell a Christmas story, right?

712
00:39:07,774 --> 00:39:10,822
I want it to capture the meaning
of Christmas, how it feels,

713
00:39:10,822 --> 00:39:13,828
I want it to be a perfect blend
of the past and present.

714
00:39:14,204 --> 00:39:15,749
It's a lot of pressure for
a tree, isn't it?

715
00:39:15,749 --> 00:39:19,297
Yes and no, okay?
Listen, I like my designs to tell a tale

716
00:39:19,297 --> 00:39:23,263
and even if I don't have it completely
figured out yet, I...

717
00:39:24,683 --> 00:39:27,438
We should get a tree for this place,
a 14-footer.

718
00:39:27,438 --> 00:39:29,275
You know, we could totally do that.

719
00:39:29,275 --> 00:39:31,530
14 feet? That is huge.

720
00:39:31,530 --> 00:39:34,077
Yeah. Well, go big or go home, right?
We want to make a statement.

721
00:39:34,077 --> 00:39:37,249
And I think we could put it on the sun
porch, just like nan used to.

722
00:39:37,584 --> 00:39:41,634
Oh, by the way, I spoke to Tim down
at the market and he's going to donate

723
00:39:41,634 --> 00:39:43,178
all the beverages for the fundraiser

724
00:39:43,178 --> 00:39:46,393
and the café is gonna do
the catering free of cost.

725
00:39:48,021 --> 00:39:50,484
Wow, that's... so generous.

726
00:39:50,484 --> 00:39:53,908
I know, people, they're just,
they're so eager to help.

727
00:39:54,284 --> 00:39:57,331
You know, this fundraiser really is doing
a lot of good for everybody.

728
00:39:57,331 --> 00:39:59,460
I guess so.

729
00:40:00,087 --> 00:40:01,214
It just feels right.

730
00:40:01,716 --> 00:40:03,678
Yeah.

731
00:40:07,936 --> 00:40:11,736
I'm gonna go get some decorations,
maybe I'll get some inspiration.

732
00:40:12,403 --> 00:40:18,833
Yes. I will take some pictures
and maybe I'll get inspired.

733
00:40:34,322 --> 00:40:35,700
Hm...

734
00:40:44,760 --> 00:40:46,680
Hm.

735
00:40:54,362 --> 00:40:56,867
Hey, Ryan?

736
00:40:57,661 --> 00:40:59,790
What's up?

737
00:40:59,790 --> 00:41:01,669
What are you doing tonight?

738
00:41:01,669 --> 00:41:03,965
Want to decorate a Christmas
tree with me?

739
00:41:07,221 --> 00:41:09,601
You have the whole town support.

740
00:41:09,601 --> 00:41:11,897
Yes, I agree.

741
00:41:11,897 --> 00:41:14,152
Okay. Chat soon.

742
00:41:15,780 --> 00:41:19,245
Apparently, Grace and Olivia have gotten
everything off the ground

743
00:41:19,245 --> 00:41:22,293
for Ryan's Ribbons and Bows
Christmas Fundraiser.

744
00:41:22,293 --> 00:41:24,297
He actually sounded excited.

745
00:41:24,297 --> 00:41:26,635
- Was that him on the phone?
- Oh, yes.

746
00:41:26,635 --> 00:41:30,768
He asked me to get the word out,
do some publicity.

747
00:41:30,768 --> 00:41:33,691
Hmm. Sounds like he wants one last
hurrah before he sells the place.

748
00:41:33,691 --> 00:41:35,319
Sells the place?

749
00:41:35,319 --> 00:41:37,198
Mm-hmm, I'm gonna make
him a great offer,

750
00:41:37,198 --> 00:41:38,325
and then you, Madame Mayor,

751
00:41:38,325 --> 00:41:41,080
will have a site for those luxury
condos we discussed.

752
00:41:41,080 --> 00:41:43,293
I'd have to see the proposal first.

753
00:41:43,293 --> 00:41:45,840
- You know that a first-class state-of
- the-art condo complex

754
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:47,636
would be great for local business.

755
00:41:47,636 --> 00:41:50,349
Just think about all of the money that
would be poured into Ivy Glen's

756
00:41:50,349 --> 00:41:53,396
restaurants and shops...
- I've already said I liked your pitch.

757
00:41:53,396 --> 00:41:55,985
...By residents enjoying the new
luxury amenities.

758
00:41:57,321 --> 00:41:59,534
We both know that the site of
the St. Nicholas House

759
00:41:59,534 --> 00:42:02,039
is quite literally the perfect location.

760
00:42:03,668 --> 00:42:08,051
Point is, I think this could be
exactly what we both need.

761
00:42:08,844 --> 00:42:12,017
I mean, you want a second term
as mayor, right, Sami?

762
00:42:12,017 --> 00:42:13,854
Boost the local economy,

763
00:42:13,854 --> 00:42:15,900
increase the tax base
and you’re a shoo-in.

764
00:42:15,900 --> 00:42:20,660
Okay. Okay, let's talk about
this more at the office tomorrow.

765
00:42:20,660 --> 00:42:22,204
I want to see those
numbers again.

766
00:42:22,204 --> 00:42:25,002
Okay. Thank you, Sami.
Oh, no, no, I got it. Thank you.

767
00:42:25,002 --> 00:42:26,922
Thank you.

768
00:42:32,601 --> 00:42:35,355
That is a great tree.

769
00:42:35,355 --> 00:42:37,694
It is gonna take us forever
to decorate it.

770
00:42:37,694 --> 00:42:39,573
Oh, I have a plan.

771
00:42:39,573 --> 00:42:42,119
I'm going to tie together the old
and the new,

772
00:42:42,119 --> 00:42:44,625
figured Mayor Hoffman
and all of the donors will love it.

773
00:42:45,375 --> 00:42:46,754
Hey.
- Where do you want this?

774
00:42:46,754 --> 00:42:48,465
Over by the tree would be great.

775
00:42:48,465 --> 00:42:50,052
Right away, boss.

776
00:42:50,052 --> 00:42:51,262
Thanks.

777
00:42:51,262 --> 00:42:53,350
What?
- Nothing.

778
00:42:54,936 --> 00:42:57,817
- Thank you all for coming.
- Alright, let's do this!

779
00:43:00,030 --> 00:43:02,326
You can take these over there and work
on that side of the tree

780
00:43:02,326 --> 00:43:03,871
and I'll have the crew
finish the top.

781
00:43:03,871 --> 00:43:06,084
- Sounds good.
- Thanks.

782
00:43:08,046 --> 00:43:10,843
This looks phenomenal.

783
00:43:10,843 --> 00:43:14,559
Yeah! Wait till you see how the design
ties in to the one at St. Nicholas House.

784
00:43:14,559 --> 00:43:17,272
Spreading the themes across locations,
I like it.

785
00:43:17,272 --> 00:43:19,903
Yeah. I just thought it might
encourage giving.

786
00:43:20,278 --> 00:43:22,867
And these are so gorgeous,
where did they come from?

787
00:43:22,867 --> 00:43:24,705
Oh, I might have had something
to do with that.

788
00:43:24,705 --> 00:43:26,542
- Ryan!
- Jack.

789
00:43:26,875 --> 00:43:30,173
By the way, I'm so sorry I missed
the wedding, guys. Congratulations.

790
00:43:30,173 --> 00:43:32,386
No, we missed you,
but we understand, you're busy.

791
00:43:32,386 --> 00:43:36,645
Yeah, but I'm always busy
and that needs to change.

792
00:43:39,191 --> 00:43:40,903
Okay, I gotta go back
to the tree.

793
00:43:40,903 --> 00:43:42,489
Yeah, I'll meet you over there
in a second.

794
00:43:42,489 --> 00:43:46,623
I'm going to get the samples for
the Peterson tree. Do you need anything?

795
00:43:47,458 --> 00:43:50,882
Grace? Do you need anything?
- No, I'm good.

796
00:43:50,882 --> 00:43:52,009
Okay.

797
00:43:52,009 --> 00:43:53,637
Bye.

798
00:43:55,015 --> 00:43:57,770
So, things went well at St. Nicholas House
this morning?

799
00:43:57,770 --> 00:44:01,194
- Yeah. Yeah... you could say that.

800
00:44:01,194 --> 00:44:04,033
I mean, so well that he lent
you his nan's decorations.

801
00:44:04,033 --> 00:44:05,452
Hmm.

802
00:44:05,452 --> 00:44:08,751
Did you see any hanging
decorations that you liked?

803
00:44:08,751 --> 00:44:13,218
Like greenery, festive greenery, no?
- Well, well, well, look at all this!

804
00:44:13,218 --> 00:44:15,765
- Hey.
- Hey! I was just in the neighbourhood,

805
00:44:15,765 --> 00:44:17,351
thought I'd pop by.
- Oh.

806
00:44:17,351 --> 00:44:19,355
Okay. Well, I'm gonna go see if
the crew needs help.

807
00:44:19,355 --> 00:44:21,735
Okay, thank you. What's this?

808
00:44:21,735 --> 00:44:24,616
Coffee. Five creams,
nine sugars.

809
00:44:24,616 --> 00:44:26,578
It's good, right?
Yeah, it's my go-to.

810
00:44:26,578 --> 00:44:27,789
Hmm.

811
00:44:27,789 --> 00:44:30,460
Anyway, I gotta run, the proposal goes
live this afternoon.

812
00:44:30,460 --> 00:44:32,549
- Oh, good luck with that.
- Thanks.

813
00:44:32,549 --> 00:44:36,222
Thanks. If it all goes well,
it could change all of our lives.

814
00:44:36,222 --> 00:44:37,307
Yeah.

815
00:44:37,307 --> 00:44:41,440
Anyway, I just wanted to say, this has
been a lot of fun,

816
00:44:41,440 --> 00:44:44,698
us reconnecting and hanging out,
just like high school.

817
00:44:44,698 --> 00:44:46,117
Yeah. Um...

818
00:44:47,579 --> 00:44:49,331
...listen, about that, Quinn,

819
00:44:49,331 --> 00:44:52,379
I think that you're a
really great guy, okay?

820
00:44:52,379 --> 00:44:56,638
And I love your drive and your
ambition and...

821
00:44:56,638 --> 00:44:59,561
I just...

822
00:44:59,561 --> 00:45:02,274
I don't think that I can do this anymore.

823
00:45:02,274 --> 00:45:06,490
I... I've really enjoyed spending
time with you, I have, but I...

824
00:45:07,200 --> 00:45:09,873
I think I'm just looking for
something a little more serious.

825
00:45:13,046 --> 00:45:14,674
Oh.

826
00:45:14,674 --> 00:45:16,595
Oh, I see, um...

827
00:45:18,974 --> 00:45:24,401
To be honest, I'm not sure I'm in a place
to settle down right now.

828
00:45:24,401 --> 00:45:27,742
I mean, I really like you, I do,

829
00:45:27,742 --> 00:45:30,288
I think you're an amazing woman,
but...

830
00:45:30,915 --> 00:45:33,419
I feel like I have so much going on.

831
00:45:34,254 --> 00:45:35,549
I... I feel like I need to focus

832
00:45:35,549 --> 00:45:37,553
right now, I hope you understand.
- Yeah, your projects.

833
00:45:37,553 --> 00:45:38,806
- Yeah.
- Oh, yeah.

834
00:45:38,806 --> 00:45:41,018
Yeah, it's gonna be huge.
I mean, bigger than...

835
00:45:42,229 --> 00:45:45,945
...than the hockey team making it to
the state championship our senior year.

836
00:45:45,945 --> 00:45:48,324
- Wow. Quinn, that is really, really big.
- Right?

837
00:45:48,324 --> 00:45:50,120
Yeah, mm-hmm.

838
00:45:50,120 --> 00:45:52,583
I've... I've really enjoyed
our time together.

839
00:45:52,917 --> 00:45:56,758
If you do change your mind,
I'm down for a dinner.

840
00:45:56,758 --> 00:45:59,263
- Oh.
- Or a heist movie.

841
00:46:00,473 --> 00:46:04,273
Or maybe even a romcom.
- Okay, deal. Good luck today.

842
00:46:04,273 --> 00:46:06,653
- Thanks.
- Yeah. Thanks for this.

843
00:46:12,205 --> 00:46:14,209
Listen, thank you so much for
your help today.

844
00:46:14,209 --> 00:46:16,798
We quite literally could not have
done that without you, Ryan.

845
00:46:16,798 --> 00:46:18,176
I'm happy to help.

846
00:46:18,176 --> 00:46:22,100
Oh, also, I wanted to give you guys this.
- Oh.

847
00:46:22,100 --> 00:46:24,981
That should cover any of the expenses.
I know you said that all the food

848
00:46:24,981 --> 00:46:28,112
and beverages were completely donated,
but I don't want to put anyone out.

849
00:46:28,112 --> 00:46:30,408
We're not doing this halfway,
so anything we don't use,

850
00:46:30,408 --> 00:46:31,995
we can donate to the food bank.

851
00:46:31,995 --> 00:46:33,624
It's incredibly generous.

852
00:46:33,624 --> 00:46:36,546
Oh, sorry, I gotta run. Grace,
this is the Gregsons

853
00:46:36,546 --> 00:46:38,926
about us potentially redoing their
kitchen and living room.

854
00:46:38,926 --> 00:46:41,180
- Yeah, I can come with you.
- No, no, no, you stay, I got it.

855
00:46:41,180 --> 00:46:43,017
Okay. Our samples are on my desk.

856
00:46:43,017 --> 00:46:46,023
Okay, amazing. Thank you. Bye.
You kids have fun!

857
00:46:46,023 --> 00:46:47,944
- Thank you for this.

858
00:46:47,944 --> 00:46:50,114
- It's what my nan would have wanted.
- Yeah.

859
00:46:50,114 --> 00:46:51,701
And you know what?

860
00:46:51,701 --> 00:46:55,500
She'd be proud having all of her
decorations in Town Square on the tree.

861
00:46:55,500 --> 00:46:56,628
Mm-hmm.

862
00:46:56,628 --> 00:46:57,964
She loved it here.

863
00:46:59,049 --> 00:47:01,011
So, what gave you the idea to do this?

864
00:47:01,011 --> 00:47:05,061
Oh. Well, I found this

865
00:47:05,061 --> 00:47:11,073
and I thought it was the perfect blend
tying together the past and present.

866
00:47:12,869 --> 00:47:16,835
Should we get back to it?
- Uh... yeah, okay.

867
00:47:17,169 --> 00:47:21,343
Actually, you know what? I have
a few errands I need to run, so...

868
00:47:21,343 --> 00:47:23,599
Yeah, okay. I don't want to take
advantage of your free labour,

869
00:47:23,599 --> 00:47:25,686
but it has been very helpful.

870
00:47:26,813 --> 00:47:28,650
Listen, if you want to get that
dinner later...

871
00:47:28,650 --> 00:47:30,403
if you're still interested.

872
00:47:30,863 --> 00:47:34,662
Oh... yeah, no, we'll talk
about that tomorrow.

873
00:47:35,873 --> 00:47:39,004
Yeah. Tomorrow, okay. Great.

874
00:48:07,352 --> 00:48:09,524
- Ryan? Hi.
- Jack.

875
00:48:09,524 --> 00:48:10,651
What can I do for you?

876
00:48:10,651 --> 00:48:13,740
I just wanted to drop this off,
Grace left it in Town Square.

877
00:48:13,740 --> 00:48:17,581
Uh... she'll be grateful for that.
She'd be lost without this thing.

878
00:48:17,581 --> 00:48:20,504
I keep trying to tell her to go
digital, but nope.

879
00:48:20,504 --> 00:48:21,756
Sounds like Grace.

880
00:48:21,756 --> 00:48:23,467
You hungry? I was just
about to order pizza.

881
00:48:23,467 --> 00:48:24,554
Oh, I couldn't interrupt.

882
00:48:24,554 --> 00:48:26,766
No, come on, I’d be grateful
for the break.

883
00:48:27,183 --> 00:48:29,062
Okay, let's do it.

884
00:48:30,398 --> 00:48:32,068
I do not remember that.

885
00:48:32,068 --> 00:48:34,031
Well, yeah, because you
already graduated.

886
00:48:34,031 --> 00:48:36,243
You were too cool to hang out
with these lowly sophomores.

887
00:48:36,243 --> 00:48:37,454
Well, that's not true!

888
00:48:38,164 --> 00:48:41,420
Okay, that's partially true,
but I was wrong.

889
00:48:41,420 --> 00:48:45,094
Now, I'm married to my sister's best
friend, working for both of them.

890
00:48:45,094 --> 00:48:46,472
And what a pair they are.

891
00:48:46,472 --> 00:48:49,896
A powerhouse dynamic duo.
I'm lucky to be in her orbit.

892
00:48:51,190 --> 00:48:53,486
So, are you enjoying being home?

893
00:48:53,486 --> 00:48:55,616
Yeah, I am.

894
00:48:56,200 --> 00:48:58,872
I was a little nervous coming back,
but... mm-hmm.

895
00:48:59,289 --> 00:49:01,335
Well, you did wait long enough.

896
00:49:01,335 --> 00:49:04,884
I didn't mean to, it's just the years
kept piling on and before I knew it...

897
00:49:05,803 --> 00:49:08,099
wow, yeah, 15 years.

898
00:49:08,099 --> 00:49:10,394
Do you regret any of it?

899
00:49:11,355 --> 00:49:14,695
Honestly, no, because it got
to where I am today,

900
00:49:14,695 --> 00:49:18,202
and yes, I love my job, but...

901
00:49:19,454 --> 00:49:21,876
You want someone to share it all with.

902
00:49:25,425 --> 00:49:27,721
When did you get so sentimental?

903
00:49:27,721 --> 00:49:29,266
I just think that as you get older,

904
00:49:29,266 --> 00:49:32,063
you start to realize what really
matters in life.

905
00:49:32,063 --> 00:49:34,151
I mean, sure, success is great,

906
00:49:34,151 --> 00:49:37,867
but if you don't have someone to share
it with, what does it matter?

907
00:49:39,286 --> 00:49:41,624
A little cheesy, but you're right.

908
00:49:41,624 --> 00:49:44,171
At the end of the day,
it's all about connection.

909
00:49:46,341 --> 00:49:48,513
How's working with your spouse?

910
00:49:48,513 --> 00:49:51,435
It's not for everyone,
I'll give you that, but for us...

911
00:49:53,147 --> 00:49:55,986
she's my best friend,
a co-pilot.

912
00:49:58,073 --> 00:49:59,535
You're really lucky.

913
00:49:59,535 --> 00:50:02,040
But don't get me wrong,
it takes work.

914
00:50:02,040 --> 00:50:06,215
But without her,
none of it matters.

915
00:50:07,927 --> 00:50:10,849
You and Grace seem to be hitting
it off again.

916
00:50:10,849 --> 00:50:13,229
Liv’s always thought you two
would end up together.

917
00:50:13,229 --> 00:50:15,233
Really?
What makes her say that?

918
00:50:15,233 --> 00:50:17,738
Grace has always been more
herself around you,

919
00:50:17,738 --> 00:50:20,577
plus, I think the best relationships
start as friendships.

920
00:50:21,704 --> 00:50:26,421
Well, I'm happy she found someone,
even if it is with Quinn.

921
00:50:27,423 --> 00:50:32,058
Okay, one, I love that your rivalry
with Quinn is alive and well

922
00:50:32,058 --> 00:50:35,941
all these years later, and two, trust me,
I know my sister,

923
00:50:35,941 --> 00:50:37,611
there's nothing going on with that guy.

924
00:50:38,320 --> 00:50:41,953
She said the same to me,
but when I saw them at the tree...

925
00:50:42,370 --> 00:50:45,627
I don't know, kind of seem like
the opposite to me.

926
00:50:45,627 --> 00:50:49,134
And he's very...
Handsome? Tall? Charming?

927
00:50:49,134 --> 00:50:51,848
I was gonna say kind,
but yeah, that works.

928
00:50:52,223 --> 00:50:53,893
It's been really nice, having him back.

929
00:50:53,893 --> 00:50:55,772
- It is, isn't it?
- Yeah.

930
00:50:55,772 --> 00:50:57,860
Do you know how long
he's staying?

931
00:50:57,860 --> 00:50:59,279
Let me talk to Grace about that.

932
00:50:59,279 --> 00:51:02,661
No, you do not need to talk to
Grace about that.

933
00:51:02,661 --> 00:51:04,874
- Talk to me about what?

934
00:51:04,874 --> 00:51:06,460
- Oh.
- Your love life.

935
00:51:06,460 --> 00:51:07,880
- Gee, thanks.

936
00:51:09,007 --> 00:51:11,011
Hey, Ryan.
What are you doing here?

937
00:51:11,011 --> 00:51:12,681
He stopped by to give you
your sketch book.

938
00:51:12,681 --> 00:51:15,227
Yeah, you...
left this at Town Square.

939
00:51:15,227 --> 00:51:17,566
Oh, thank you so much,
you're a lifesaver.

940
00:51:17,566 --> 00:51:20,154
Okay. Jack, we gotta go.
Remember?

941
00:51:20,154 --> 00:51:21,949
- We do?
- Yeah!

942
00:51:21,949 --> 00:51:24,538
Bye. See you both later.
- Woah...

943
00:51:24,538 --> 00:51:27,085
...did I forget something?

944
00:51:27,085 --> 00:51:30,884
Do we forget... do you have my coat?
- I have your coat, let's go.

945
00:51:33,097 --> 00:51:34,767
Uh...

946
00:51:34,767 --> 00:51:36,562
Okay. Um...

947
00:51:36,896 --> 00:51:40,111
I don't know about you, but I could
go for a sugar cookie, right now.

948
00:51:40,111 --> 00:51:41,572
- Okay, sure.

949
00:51:41,572 --> 00:51:43,450
Alright.

950
00:51:44,160 --> 00:51:45,956
- I can't believe we're doing this.

951
00:51:45,956 --> 00:51:48,168
I mean, we're actually gonna
have cookies for dinner.

952
00:51:48,168 --> 00:51:51,551
- Are you mad at it?
- I mean... no, of course not.

953
00:51:51,551 --> 00:51:53,972
Hey, are you sure everything in
this kitchen still works?

954
00:51:53,972 --> 00:51:55,684
Oh, for sure. I got a maintenance team

955
00:51:55,684 --> 00:51:58,105
here all the time making sure everything
is in working order.

956
00:51:58,105 --> 00:52:00,902
Gotta protect your investments.
- Investments? What does that mean?

957
00:52:00,902 --> 00:52:04,325
You know, yeah, it's my family
house, but it's also an asset.

958
00:52:04,325 --> 00:52:06,329
Oh.

959
00:52:06,914 --> 00:52:09,502
- What?
- Hmm.

960
00:52:09,837 --> 00:52:12,467
Uh... that eyebrow raise begs to differ.

961
00:52:13,636 --> 00:52:17,936
It's just an asset? I mean, come on,
is that really how you see this place?

962
00:52:19,147 --> 00:52:21,819
That’s what owning property
is, right?

963
00:52:21,819 --> 00:52:24,950
- Let's make some cookies, hmm?
- Okay.

964
00:52:27,706 --> 00:52:29,585
Okay, so first of all, if you're gonna
help me with this,

965
00:52:29,585 --> 00:52:31,338
you might want to take
off your suit jacket.

966
00:52:31,338 --> 00:52:33,300
- Um... okay. Yeah, you're right.

967
00:52:33,300 --> 00:52:34,845
Sorry, it's just a habit.

968
00:52:34,845 --> 00:52:36,682
It's your suit of armour, huh?

969
00:52:37,643 --> 00:52:40,732
Exactly, yes, a suit of armour.

970
00:52:40,732 --> 00:52:42,485
Okay, so tell me about your work.

971
00:52:42,485 --> 00:52:45,074
Um... well, basically,
I'm a financial advisor,

972
00:52:45,074 --> 00:52:47,704
I help people achieve their
long-term financial goals

973
00:52:47,704 --> 00:52:49,499
in the shortest time possible.

974
00:52:49,834 --> 00:52:52,421
Oh. Sounds fun. Do you like it?

975
00:52:52,421 --> 00:52:54,510
Yeah, I actually do.

976
00:52:54,510 --> 00:52:57,431
It's really rewarding when I see
the look on my client's face

977
00:52:57,431 --> 00:53:00,229
when I help them reach their goals
and I double their investment.

978
00:53:00,689 --> 00:53:02,275
Great.

979
00:53:02,651 --> 00:53:06,701
Alright, so all you have to do
is just, you're gonna take this,

980
00:53:06,701 --> 00:53:09,330
put a little flour on there and you're
gonna give it some easy pressure

981
00:53:09,330 --> 00:53:10,542
back and forth.

982
00:53:10,542 --> 00:53:11,836
Here you go.

983
00:53:11,836 --> 00:53:12,921
Okay.

984
00:53:12,921 --> 00:53:14,842
Like that?
- Yeah.

985
00:53:14,842 --> 00:53:15,969
Okay.

986
00:53:15,969 --> 00:53:18,307
So, how long are you staying
in town?

987
00:53:18,307 --> 00:53:22,148
I don't know. This fundraiser is keeping
me here a bit longer and to be honest,

988
00:53:22,148 --> 00:53:24,152
I'm not that mad at it.

989
00:53:24,152 --> 00:53:25,780
I'm kind of enjoying being back.

990
00:53:25,780 --> 00:53:28,745
Oh, "Actually enjoying being back."
Well, what were you expecting?

991
00:53:28,745 --> 00:53:32,376
Well, I don't know. I didn't know what
I was walking into, it's been so long.

992
00:53:33,086 --> 00:53:35,382
Well, are you happy with what you found?

993
00:53:36,719 --> 00:53:38,430
Surprisingly, yeah.

994
00:53:38,430 --> 00:53:41,186
Makes me want to spend more time here.
I don't think I'm doing this right.

995
00:53:41,186 --> 00:53:42,898
- I'll take over.

996
00:53:42,898 --> 00:53:44,777
- Yeah.
- Do you have cookie cutters?

997
00:53:44,777 --> 00:53:47,950
Uh... yeah, I think so. Just...

998
00:53:51,874 --> 00:53:53,586
Oh, here we go.
- Perfect.

999
00:53:53,586 --> 00:53:55,715
There is so much junk in this house.

1000
00:53:55,715 --> 00:53:59,430
Junk? Listen, I happen to think that
there's a lot of things with sentimental

1001
00:53:59,430 --> 00:54:01,309
value in this house.

1002
00:54:01,309 --> 00:54:03,438
So, what are your plans for this
house anyway, uh?

1003
00:54:03,438 --> 00:54:07,656
I mean, it's such a magical place,
it makes me sad to think about it empty.

1004
00:54:07,656 --> 00:54:13,041
Me too. You're right, I'm not doing this
place justice, my nan loved this place.

1005
00:54:13,041 --> 00:54:14,753
I know she did.

1006
00:54:17,383 --> 00:54:19,847
I should have brought her back
for one last Christmas.

1007
00:54:20,305 --> 00:54:24,397
No. Hey, you look at me,
Ryan St. Nicholas, okay?

1008
00:54:25,065 --> 00:54:29,198
I know that it was not an easy decision,
moving your nan away from this place,

1009
00:54:29,742 --> 00:54:34,835
but I also know you and I know
that you took great care of her.

1010
00:54:35,754 --> 00:54:37,841
You know what?
What you're doing right now,

1011
00:54:37,841 --> 00:54:41,640
reviving her legacy with
the Ribbons and Bows Fundraiser,

1012
00:54:41,640 --> 00:54:43,393
that would make her very,
very proud.

1013
00:54:44,228 --> 00:54:45,481
- Thank you.
- Mm-hmm.

1014
00:54:45,481 --> 00:54:46,942
You're... you're right.

1015
00:54:46,942 --> 00:54:49,656
Yeah. Alright, you want to cut
some cookies?

1016
00:54:49,656 --> 00:54:51,159
- Yes.
- Great.

1017
00:54:51,159 --> 00:54:54,165
Okay. Ooh, I'll grab this one
right here.

1018
00:54:54,165 --> 00:54:55,585
Perfect.

1019
00:54:58,758 --> 00:55:00,302
Alright.

1020
00:55:01,262 --> 00:55:03,559
How did I do?

1021
00:55:03,559 --> 00:55:05,062
Nailed it!

1022
00:55:05,062 --> 00:55:07,567
Hopefully, it tastes better
than it looks.

1023
00:55:07,567 --> 00:55:09,237
It's the moment of truth.

1024
00:55:11,700 --> 00:55:14,873
I can confirm, it does.

1025
00:55:14,873 --> 00:55:19,675
A plus on your baking skills and
C minus for my decorating skills.

1026
00:55:19,675 --> 00:55:22,889
Hey, no, I would give that
a solid B minus.

1027
00:55:22,889 --> 00:55:24,685
Uh-huh, that's generous.

1028
00:55:27,022 --> 00:55:28,985
Oh, sorry, it's my tree guy.

1029
00:55:28,985 --> 00:55:30,905
- You got a tree guy?
- Yeah.

1030
00:55:31,532 --> 00:55:35,163
Hey, Billy. Did you get my
message about the tree earlier? Mm-hmm.

1031
00:55:35,163 --> 00:55:38,086
Uh... 14 feet would be ideal.

1032
00:55:39,506 --> 00:55:40,925
Oh.

1033
00:55:41,301 --> 00:55:43,430
Yeah, no, that's okay,
thanks anyway.

1034
00:55:43,430 --> 00:55:45,142
Mm-hmm. Bye.

1035
00:55:46,436 --> 00:55:47,689
Tree problems?

1036
00:55:47,689 --> 00:55:50,193
I just really wanted a 14-foot tree,

1037
00:55:50,193 --> 00:55:53,618
but all the big ones are gone within
a 50-mile radius, so...

1038
00:55:54,076 --> 00:55:56,247
...anyway, I didn't realize how late
it was getting.

1039
00:55:56,247 --> 00:55:58,669
I have a big day tomorrow,
but this was so much fun.

1040
00:55:58,669 --> 00:56:00,632
So...
- Oh, no, no, no, I got it.

1041
00:56:00,632 --> 00:56:03,470
What? No, I am not making you
clean up your entire kitchen by yourself.

1042
00:56:03,470 --> 00:56:05,098
Okay, I'll make you a deal.

1043
00:56:05,098 --> 00:56:07,729
Leave the cookies
and we're even.

1044
00:56:08,773 --> 00:56:12,530
Okay. Deal.

1045
00:56:12,530 --> 00:56:14,868
So, will I see you at the Christmas tree
lighting tomorrow?

1046
00:56:14,868 --> 00:56:16,037
I wouldn't miss it.

1047
00:56:16,037 --> 00:56:18,918
Great. Maybe we can get that
dinner we talked about.

1048
00:56:18,918 --> 00:56:20,546
Yeah, I'd like that.

1049
00:56:20,546 --> 00:56:22,132
Me too.

1050
00:56:22,132 --> 00:56:24,095
Alright.
Well, get out of here.

1051
00:56:24,095 --> 00:56:26,140
Thanks for a good night.

1052
00:56:36,578 --> 00:56:40,837
Okay, party people! We've got
T-minus three hours until showtime!

1053
00:56:43,008 --> 00:56:45,555
Hey, Jack and I are gonna grab a pizza
and watch old Christmas movies

1054
00:56:45,555 --> 00:56:47,266
after the tree lighting
if you want to join.

1055
00:56:47,266 --> 00:56:49,186
Oh, I can't, I'm having dinner
with Ryan.

1056
00:56:49,186 --> 00:56:51,734
- Wait, you're what?
- Just as friends.

1057
00:56:51,734 --> 00:56:54,363
Okay, you go home,
you do a face mask,

1058
00:56:54,363 --> 00:56:57,119
you paint your nails,
you, you give yourself a blowout.

1059
00:56:57,119 --> 00:56:59,206
You can just meet me here before
the tree lighting.

1060
00:56:59,206 --> 00:57:00,333
But we have work to do!

1061
00:57:00,333 --> 00:57:02,672
I know, I've got it covered.
You go, you go!

1062
00:57:02,672 --> 00:57:07,014
- Oh, I...
- Wear a cute dress! Wear heels!

1063
00:57:08,934 --> 00:57:11,230
Yes!

1064
00:57:12,650 --> 00:57:17,076
Oh, we are so close.
Operation Mistletoe is almost a success.

1065
00:57:17,076 --> 00:57:19,330
- Olivia...
- They are going for dinner tonight,

1066
00:57:19,330 --> 00:57:23,046
for dinner, do you hear me?
I just need to pull more sprigs.

1067
00:57:23,046 --> 00:57:26,260
- I think you need to take a breath.
- No, I need more mistletoe.

1068
00:57:26,260 --> 00:57:29,726
Do you think Grace will be angry if
she finds out that you're behind

1069
00:57:29,726 --> 00:57:32,314
all the mysterious mistletoe that keeps
popping up around town?

1070
00:57:32,314 --> 00:57:34,360
No, I think that she would thank me.

1071
00:57:34,360 --> 00:57:37,116
I mean, Christmas is the most romantic
time of the year,

1072
00:57:37,116 --> 00:57:39,036
I'm just giving them a little nudge.

1073
00:57:39,036 --> 00:57:42,000
Love you. Wish me luck!

1074
00:57:42,000 --> 00:57:44,296
Love you.

1075
00:57:59,285 --> 00:58:00,705
Hey.

1076
00:58:00,705 --> 00:58:02,291
Hi.

1077
00:58:03,586 --> 00:58:05,130
Should be any minute now.

1078
00:58:06,550 --> 00:58:09,346
Is it weird that I kind of feel like a
little kid right now?

1079
00:58:09,346 --> 00:58:11,434
- No, not at all.

1080
00:58:11,434 --> 00:58:13,814
I get excited every time I go to
a Christmas tree lighting.

1081
00:58:13,814 --> 00:58:17,279
I mean, especially when we're
the ones in charge of decorating it.

1082
00:58:17,279 --> 00:58:19,200
Yeah.

1083
00:58:20,870 --> 00:58:22,247
Do you think Sami likes it?

1084
00:58:22,832 --> 00:58:26,047
I think we'll have to wait for
the tree to be lit up to know that.

1085
00:58:27,466 --> 00:58:31,516
Hey, do you remember when we bet
that you couldn't make it

1086
00:58:31,516 --> 00:58:33,771
to the top of the Town Square
Christmas tree?

1087
00:58:33,771 --> 00:58:36,234
I can't believe you actually tried
to do it.

1088
00:58:36,234 --> 00:58:39,323
I made it halfway up that tree before
Mayor Dodds started to call my parents.

1089
00:58:39,323 --> 00:58:41,452
Yeah. Please don't do that
tonight.

1090
00:58:41,452 --> 00:58:43,331
No promises.

1091
00:58:47,005 --> 00:58:50,136
Wow! Look at that, the whole
group's here!

1092
00:58:50,136 --> 00:58:52,140
Go Polar Bears!

1093
00:58:52,642 --> 00:58:54,813
Come on, go Polar Bears!

1094
00:58:54,813 --> 00:58:56,692
Go Polar Bears.

1095
00:58:56,692 --> 00:58:58,779
- Hey, Grace.
- Quinn.

1096
00:58:59,614 --> 00:59:03,037
It's great having Santaman back, huh?

1097
00:59:03,037 --> 00:59:04,791
Yeah, it is, actually.

1098
00:59:05,417 --> 00:59:08,924
Gather round, everyone, it's
time to light the tree!

1099
00:59:09,926 --> 00:59:12,472
- Okay.

1100
00:59:22,702 --> 00:59:25,165
Merry Christmas!

1101
00:59:25,498 --> 00:59:30,760
Oh, it's so beautiful! I don't think
I've ever seen one prettier tree

1102
00:59:30,760 --> 00:59:32,805
than this Christmas tree.

1103
00:59:34,433 --> 00:59:37,940
- Oh, I think that Sami likes it.
- I think she loves it.

1104
00:59:39,736 --> 00:59:42,742
- You guys did a beautiful job.
- Thank you.

1105
00:59:43,201 --> 00:59:46,499
And huge thanks to you for all your help

1106
00:59:46,499 --> 00:59:48,461
and letting use your grandma's
decorations.

1107
00:59:48,461 --> 00:59:50,758
- I'm happy they came in handy.
- Yeah.

1108
00:59:50,758 --> 00:59:53,889
Oh, the volunteers are gonna drop by
the house tomorrow to decorate

1109
00:59:53,889 --> 00:59:55,475
based on Grace's designs.

1110
00:59:55,475 --> 00:59:57,647
Did she mention we're gonna leave
the old decorations up?

1111
00:59:57,647 --> 01:00:02,532
I want them to be part of it so we can
build upon Mrs. St. Nicholas’ legacy.

1112
01:00:02,532 --> 01:00:05,453
- I love that. I'll let them know.
- Okay.

1113
01:00:07,792 --> 01:00:11,424
You know, I think I forgot how much
I missed Christmas here.

1114
01:00:11,424 --> 01:00:13,469
Oh yeah?

1115
01:00:15,265 --> 01:00:18,271
- So, should we go eat?
- Yeah, I'm starving.

1116
01:00:18,271 --> 01:00:20,776
Oh, man, I'd love to,
I would, but I've...

1117
01:00:20,776 --> 01:00:23,699
I've got this investor thing I need to
finish, but let's talk soon.

1118
01:00:23,699 --> 01:00:25,661
I've got some things
I want to run by you.

1119
01:00:25,661 --> 01:00:27,164
Bye, Grace.
- Sure.

1120
01:00:27,164 --> 01:00:29,251
Bye, Quinn.

1121
01:00:30,420 --> 01:00:32,592
- Shall we?
- Yeah.

1122
01:00:36,223 --> 01:00:37,894
You did not say that.

1123
01:00:37,894 --> 01:00:40,566
I did. It was my first board meeting,
I had no clue what was going on.

1124
01:00:40,566 --> 01:00:44,949
Oh, come on! Even I know that you
don't comment on your boss's lunch order.

1125
01:00:44,949 --> 01:00:46,953
I thought it was helping.

1126
01:00:46,953 --> 01:00:49,876
- You can get that if you need.

1127
01:00:49,876 --> 01:00:53,174
No. That is business,
it can wait till business hours.

1128
01:00:54,009 --> 01:00:57,600
I'm sorry, who are you and what have you
done with Ryan St. Nicholas?

1129
01:00:57,600 --> 01:01:00,981
Well, it is Christmas time and since
I've been back here

1130
01:01:00,981 --> 01:01:03,820
and staying at the St. Nicholas House,
it's made me realize that maybe over

1131
01:01:03,820 --> 01:01:06,910
the past few years, my priorities have
been a bit out of whack.

1132
01:01:07,620 --> 01:01:09,498
Yeah, I can relate to that.

1133
01:01:09,498 --> 01:01:12,755
You know, my parents actually invited me
on their Christmas European backpacking

1134
01:01:12,755 --> 01:01:15,009
tour and I said no because I had to work.

1135
01:01:15,009 --> 01:01:16,136
I mean, who does that?

1136
01:01:16,136 --> 01:01:18,224
At least, Jack stayed back
with you.

1137
01:01:18,224 --> 01:01:22,817
Yeah. Yeah, but he's gonna celebrate
with Olivia and her family, so...

1138
01:01:24,278 --> 01:01:28,620
How about this? Next Christmas,
we'll plan it out,

1139
01:01:28,620 --> 01:01:30,456
we'll have a work-free
Christmas.

1140
01:01:32,837 --> 01:01:35,801
So, does that mean you're
coming back next Christmas too?

1141
01:01:39,517 --> 01:01:41,437
What?

1142
01:01:42,230 --> 01:01:45,028
To be honest, I was actually thinking
about selling the St. Nicholas House.

1143
01:01:45,821 --> 01:01:47,742
You what?

1144
01:01:48,284 --> 01:01:52,585
You were right, it's sad that it's just
been sitting there vacant all this time.

1145
01:01:54,171 --> 01:01:56,008
Yeah, but...

1146
01:01:56,008 --> 01:01:58,137
I mean, come on,
you can't just sell it.

1147
01:01:58,137 --> 01:02:00,141
Oh, I know that now.

1148
01:02:00,141 --> 01:02:04,358
I think I was just avoiding it because
of what it meant, that without my nan...

1149
01:02:04,358 --> 01:02:05,861
I'm alone, so...

1150
01:02:05,861 --> 01:02:08,825
You're not alone. Listen,
you have your friends and...

1151
01:02:09,368 --> 01:02:13,417
Ryan, no matter how far away you are,
how much time has passed

1152
01:02:13,417 --> 01:02:16,883
or wherever life takes us,
you'll always have me.

1153
01:02:17,635 --> 01:02:19,722
You know that.

1154
01:02:20,808 --> 01:02:22,770
I missed you, Grace.

1155
01:02:23,730 --> 01:02:25,567
I missed you too, Ryan.

1156
01:02:32,122 --> 01:02:35,044
We're not technically under it.

1157
01:02:35,044 --> 01:02:39,219
You're right. Technically,
the bar is under it.

1158
01:02:39,219 --> 01:02:40,597
Yeah.

1159
01:02:42,727 --> 01:02:44,438
Can I walk you home?

1160
01:02:44,438 --> 01:02:46,526
Sure, I'd love that.

1161
01:02:53,122 --> 01:02:54,959
Hey, can you do me a favour?

1162
01:02:54,959 --> 01:02:56,170
Of course.

1163
01:02:56,170 --> 01:02:59,552
Can you promise not to wait so long next
time before you come back home?

1164
01:02:59,552 --> 01:03:02,098
- I won't.
- Okay, good.

1165
01:03:02,432 --> 01:03:05,313
Alright, if you had to watch one
Christmas movie

1166
01:03:05,313 --> 01:03:07,192
for the rest of your life,
what would it be?

1167
01:03:07,192 --> 01:03:08,862
Easy, A Christmas Carol.

1168
01:03:08,862 --> 01:03:10,406
Really? Why?

1169
01:03:10,406 --> 01:03:13,329
Because it has a lot
of important lessons in it.

1170
01:03:13,329 --> 01:03:16,126
What, like, "Don't count your money
every day, all day,

1171
01:03:16,126 --> 01:03:18,088
or your Christmas
spirit will be zapped?"

1172
01:03:18,088 --> 01:03:21,094
More like, "Anyone can change their life

1173
01:03:21,094 --> 01:03:24,519
and no matter where you are,
choices you made, you can pivot."

1174
01:03:25,102 --> 01:03:27,858
Wow! Says the boy who thought
his life would be over

1175
01:03:27,858 --> 01:03:29,946
if he didn't make valedictorian.

1176
01:03:29,946 --> 01:03:31,908
Well, thankfully, I didn't
peak in high school.

1177
01:03:33,077 --> 01:03:34,789
Speaking of high school.
- Mm-hmm.

1178
01:03:34,789 --> 01:03:37,545
When is the last time you went
pranking?

1179
01:03:37,545 --> 01:03:39,381
You mean like what Quinn
and Olivia used to do

1180
01:03:39,381 --> 01:03:41,511
with the giant ornaments in our yard?

1181
01:03:42,053 --> 01:03:44,725
I can safely say it's been
years, why?

1182
01:03:44,725 --> 01:03:47,272
Because it's my favourite
thing to do during the holidays.

1183
01:03:47,272 --> 01:03:48,817
- Oh yeah?
- And I think we should do it.

1184
01:03:48,817 --> 01:03:51,906
Are you in? Are you... yeah? Okay.

1185
01:03:55,998 --> 01:03:59,004
Oh, Quinn has done a lot with
his parents' old place.

1186
01:03:59,004 --> 01:04:00,674
You know, he is a real estate
developer.

1187
01:04:00,674 --> 01:04:03,345
I know, but I always thought he would do
something in high school

1188
01:04:03,345 --> 01:04:04,932
so he'd never have to leave.

1189
01:04:04,932 --> 01:04:06,226
You know he never misses a game?

1190
01:04:07,228 --> 01:04:09,232
Yeah, that makes sense.

1191
01:04:09,232 --> 01:04:10,861
You ever go with him?

1192
01:04:10,861 --> 01:04:14,367
Yeah, the homecoming
a few times... a bunch of us.

1193
01:04:14,367 --> 01:04:15,704
Hmm.

1194
01:04:15,704 --> 01:04:18,500
Do you remember when we TPd
his house seven nights in a row?

1195
01:04:18,500 --> 01:04:22,216
The last night, his dad was waiting
for us, sitting in the window.

1196
01:04:23,762 --> 01:04:26,350
Quinn told me he loved it,
made him feel important.

1197
01:04:26,350 --> 01:04:27,728
- Really?
- Yeah.

1198
01:04:27,728 --> 01:04:30,567
That's so cute. Oh.

1199
01:04:30,567 --> 01:04:32,821
I'm sorry Olivia is missing this.

1200
01:04:34,324 --> 01:04:37,330
I don't know, I kinda like
that it's just the two of us.

1201
01:04:38,165 --> 01:04:39,669
(nervous chuckle

1202
01:04:39,669 --> 01:04:43,300
Okay, let's go.
- Shush! Gotta be quiet.

1203
01:04:44,219 --> 01:04:46,599
Shush!

1204
01:04:46,599 --> 01:04:48,520
Shush.

1205
01:04:49,437 --> 01:04:51,609
- It's magnificent.

1206
01:04:51,609 --> 01:04:53,738
Oh, I wish I could see his
face in the morning.

1207
01:04:53,738 --> 01:04:55,909
- I know he's gonna feel so important.
- Sssh.

1208
01:04:55,909 --> 01:04:58,832
Let's get out of here,
we have to go!

1209
01:04:58,832 --> 01:05:00,752
Run!

1210
01:05:11,566 --> 01:05:14,070
Okay, thanks. Bye.

1211
01:05:14,822 --> 01:05:16,701
- What was that?

1212
01:05:16,701 --> 01:05:19,497
Still no dice on the 14-foot tree
for St. Nicholas House,

1213
01:05:19,497 --> 01:05:23,297
but I stayed up all night last night
and I was able to finalize the design.

1214
01:05:23,297 --> 01:05:25,635
Oh, it looks like something
from A Christmas Carol.

1215
01:05:25,635 --> 01:05:28,265
Thanks. It's going for a Charles
Dickens' Christmas,

1216
01:05:28,265 --> 01:05:29,643
Ribbons and Bows edition.

1217
01:05:29,643 --> 01:05:31,271
Tall order, but I love it.

1218
01:05:31,271 --> 01:05:33,985
I just want it to be special
for his nan.

1219
01:05:33,985 --> 01:05:35,530
Not for him?

1220
01:05:36,783 --> 01:05:38,077
- Hey!
- Hey.

1221
01:05:38,077 --> 01:05:39,370
Hi.

1222
01:05:39,370 --> 01:05:42,126
I was just about to head over to
your house. The volunteers will be there

1223
01:05:42,126 --> 01:05:43,378
any minute to help us decorate.

1224
01:05:43,378 --> 01:05:46,093
Oh, okay. Well, I'll give you a ride.
I have another surprise for you.

1225
01:05:46,093 --> 01:05:47,513
Great.

1226
01:05:53,650 --> 01:05:55,946
Okay, you don't need to gloat.

1227
01:05:55,946 --> 01:06:00,371
I'm not gloating, this is good.
This is good.

1228
01:06:00,956 --> 01:06:02,876
I need mistletoe.

1229
01:06:04,420 --> 01:06:06,341
Okay.

1230
01:06:07,051 --> 01:06:10,141
What's all this about?
- It's your surprise.

1231
01:06:10,851 --> 01:06:12,186
You said 14 feet, right?

1232
01:06:12,186 --> 01:06:14,984
How did you...
where did you...

1233
01:06:14,984 --> 01:06:17,071
You're not the only one with
a tree guy.

1234
01:06:17,071 --> 01:06:18,700
Oh!

1235
01:06:20,871 --> 01:06:23,041
Okay, but you're sure
it's 14 feet?

1236
01:06:23,041 --> 01:06:24,169
Better be.

1237
01:06:24,169 --> 01:06:26,381
Gosh, I'm gonna cry.

1238
01:06:31,601 --> 01:06:37,153
11, 12, 13, 14! It's perfect.
Perfect!

1239
01:06:37,153 --> 01:06:39,575
Oh, my goodness.
- You guys nailed it.

1240
01:06:39,575 --> 01:06:42,664
Okay. They will help you put
it wherever you want.

1241
01:06:42,664 --> 01:06:46,463
Uh... how about on the sun porch,
where nan used to put it?

1242
01:06:46,964 --> 01:06:48,217
Yeah.

1243
01:06:48,676 --> 01:06:52,559
Um... if you put it on the sun porch,
pretty please. Thank you.

1244
01:06:52,559 --> 01:06:54,437
I can't believe you did this.

1245
01:06:54,437 --> 01:06:56,233
Oh, you know, always happy
to help.

1246
01:06:56,233 --> 01:06:57,819
Now, we just gotta decorate the thing.

1247
01:06:57,819 --> 01:07:01,869
Okay, so I was thinking, A Christmas
Carol is your favourite movie, right?

1248
01:07:01,869 --> 01:07:03,790
So I used that to finalize my design
last night

1249
01:07:03,790 --> 01:07:06,963
and I was thinking that's the perfect
blend of old and new.

1250
01:07:06,963 --> 01:07:09,677
It signifies change, but also...
- How some things stay the same?

1251
01:07:09,677 --> 01:07:10,929
Yes.

1252
01:07:10,929 --> 01:07:14,979
But the real question is,
"Can we pull it off?"

1253
01:07:15,479 --> 01:07:18,569
Um... oh, I think we can, Ryan
St. Nicholas, yes.

1254
01:07:19,738 --> 01:07:21,993
Hi! Hi, everyone. Oh, thank you
so much for coming.

1255
01:07:21,993 --> 01:07:23,913
We'll meet you right inside.
- Thank you, thank you.

1256
01:07:23,913 --> 01:07:26,001
- I think we can do this.
- Thank you guys.

1257
01:07:26,001 --> 01:07:27,169
- Okay.
- Let's go.

1258
01:07:27,169 --> 01:07:28,631
- Let's go decorate this house.
- After you.

1259
01:07:28,631 --> 01:07:30,426
Alright.

1260
01:07:39,193 --> 01:07:41,072
No, no, no. We... yeah, we got this.

1261
01:07:41,072 --> 01:07:44,037
The Mayor approved the plan, so we can
move forward with the deal.

1262
01:07:44,037 --> 01:07:48,253
I'm closing on the land any day, now.
Oh, yeah, it's gonna be great.

1263
01:07:48,253 --> 01:07:50,424
Go Polar Bears!

1264
01:07:57,021 --> 01:07:58,482
This one...

1265
01:07:58,482 --> 01:08:00,528
Right...

1266
01:08:00,528 --> 01:08:03,367
I think you got it.

1267
01:08:23,825 --> 01:08:26,204
Oh, thank you so much for your help.

1268
01:08:26,204 --> 01:08:28,918
Can't wait for you all to
celebrate with us tomorrow.

1269
01:08:30,379 --> 01:08:32,843
I couldn't bribe you with dinner,
could I?

1270
01:08:32,843 --> 01:08:34,095
Yeah, dinner would be great.

1271
01:08:34,095 --> 01:08:36,391
Alright. I'll find us some
takeout menus.

1272
01:08:37,309 --> 01:08:41,151
By the way, everything looks perfect,
but I'm not surprised at all.

1273
01:08:41,484 --> 01:08:43,363
Thank you.

1274
01:08:43,363 --> 01:08:44,992
Okay.

1275
01:08:45,577 --> 01:08:46,829
Where are you going?

1276
01:08:46,829 --> 01:08:49,668
I'm just gonna swing by St. Nicholas
House on the way home.

1277
01:08:49,668 --> 01:08:50,962
Why?

1278
01:08:50,962 --> 01:08:53,509
- To hang decorations.
- Olivia...

1279
01:08:53,509 --> 01:08:55,930
Grace said that they haven't kissed yet
and by my calculations,

1280
01:08:55,930 --> 01:08:57,934
they've been under
the mistletoe three time,

1281
01:08:57,934 --> 01:08:59,479
still no kiss.
We're running out of time!

1282
01:08:59,479 --> 01:09:02,694
I think it's time to give
Operation Mistletoe a rest, my love.

1283
01:09:02,694 --> 01:09:06,075
Okay. I just want to try one more thing
and then, I will, I promise.

1284
01:09:06,075 --> 01:09:07,579
He’s leaving, Liv.

1285
01:09:07,579 --> 01:09:10,417
No, not if I can convince him
he has a reason to stay.

1286
01:09:10,417 --> 01:09:13,883
Wish me luck.
- Good luck.

1287
01:09:16,429 --> 01:09:18,559
- Hello.
- Hey.

1288
01:09:19,686 --> 01:09:20,980
Wow!

1289
01:09:20,980 --> 01:09:24,530
This place looks great!

1290
01:09:24,530 --> 01:09:25,698
Thanks.

1291
01:09:26,074 --> 01:09:27,159
Really.

1292
01:09:29,623 --> 01:09:32,461
A little old school for my taste,
but still pretty nice!

1293
01:09:33,589 --> 01:09:35,133
- What can I do for you, Quinn?

1294
01:09:35,133 --> 01:09:36,637
Is Ryan around?

1295
01:09:36,637 --> 01:09:39,768
I sent him a text about some papers
I need him to sign.

1296
01:09:39,768 --> 01:09:41,564
Oh, what kind of papers?

1297
01:09:49,621 --> 01:09:51,249
Shoot!

1298
01:09:54,631 --> 01:09:55,758
Between you and me, I think...

1299
01:09:55,758 --> 01:09:58,471
I think it's time this place got a little
bit of a facelift, don't you?

1300
01:09:58,471 --> 01:10:00,518
I wasn't under the impression
he was selling.

1301
01:10:00,518 --> 01:10:02,021
Oh, no, he's definitely gonna sell.

1302
01:10:02,021 --> 01:10:06,195
Everybody has a price and
I think I might have found his.

1303
01:10:06,989 --> 01:10:11,247
Thank you for the ornaments on
the lawn, by the way.

1304
01:10:11,582 --> 01:10:13,251
Such a blast from the past.

1305
01:10:23,229 --> 01:10:25,693
- Olivia, are you okay?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

1306
01:10:25,693 --> 01:10:29,033
What are you doing here?
And what is all this?

1307
01:10:29,743 --> 01:10:32,331
- It's just...
- Mistletoe?

1308
01:10:32,999 --> 01:10:34,711
I can explain.

1309
01:10:34,711 --> 01:10:37,466
Wait, are you the one that's been
putting it all over the place?

1310
01:10:37,466 --> 01:10:40,973
- I was just trying to help.
- Help with what?

1311
01:10:40,973 --> 01:10:43,813
Oh, hey, Olivia. Were
you in on the lawn gag too?

1312
01:10:43,813 --> 01:10:45,858
The what?
- Hello, I'm back.

1313
01:10:45,858 --> 01:10:48,196
Oh, there he is.
Oh.

1314
01:10:48,196 --> 01:10:50,367
- What's going on?
- Can we talk for a second?

1315
01:10:50,367 --> 01:10:52,204
I want to run something by you
about the sale.

1316
01:10:52,204 --> 01:10:54,041
I don't know,
I haven't decided if I'm gonna...

1317
01:10:54,041 --> 01:10:58,133
What? Come on, man!
This place has sat vacant for years.

1318
01:10:58,133 --> 01:10:59,886
Sami already approved the plans.

1319
01:10:59,886 --> 01:11:02,266
Wait, Sam...

1320
01:11:02,266 --> 01:11:04,688
your project was Ryan's house?

1321
01:11:04,688 --> 01:11:07,192
You didn't think that was an important
detail to share, Quinn?

1322
01:11:07,192 --> 01:11:11,827
Picture it, okay? This place
completely demolished and its place,

1323
01:11:11,827 --> 01:11:16,461
a brand new state of the art world-class
high-end condo complex.

1324
01:11:16,461 --> 01:11:18,924
I can't wait to see your bid to decorate
the place,

1325
01:11:18,924 --> 01:11:21,012
I think it's gonna be a great
collaboration.

1326
01:11:21,012 --> 01:11:23,642
And Sami has already given us
the green light to start demo

1327
01:11:23,642 --> 01:11:25,187
at the top of the new year.

1328
01:11:25,187 --> 01:11:27,525
Bro, this place will no longer
be your burden.

1329
01:11:27,525 --> 01:11:29,863
- Okay, I'm just gonna...
- What is that?

1330
01:11:29,863 --> 01:11:33,328
Oh. You know, the mistletoe
that keeps popping up everywhere,

1331
01:11:33,328 --> 01:11:34,581
that was Olivia.

1332
01:11:34,581 --> 01:11:35,833
What mistletoe?

1333
01:11:35,833 --> 01:11:38,254
- That mistletoe, Quinn.

1334
01:11:41,804 --> 01:11:43,097
Wait, are you two...

1335
01:11:43,097 --> 01:11:46,062
is that why you cut things off
with me?

1336
01:11:48,358 --> 01:11:51,113
Grace, he's not sticking around.

1337
01:11:51,113 --> 01:11:53,994
He's about to run back
to his life in New York.

1338
01:11:54,788 --> 01:11:57,167
He's too good for Ivy Glen, remember?

1339
01:11:57,877 --> 01:12:01,092
That's why he hasn't lived here
in the last 15 years.

1340
01:12:02,136 --> 01:12:05,016
So, whatever little fantasy
he's had you wrapped up in

1341
01:12:05,016 --> 01:12:08,983
the last couple days, it's not real.

1342
01:12:10,736 --> 01:12:12,699
I bet you anything he's already
booked his flight

1343
01:12:12,699 --> 01:12:14,661
for first thing Christmas morning.

1344
01:12:14,661 --> 01:12:18,711
I mean, the only reason he came
back here was to sell the place.

1345
01:12:19,921 --> 01:12:21,007
Is that true?

1346
01:12:21,675 --> 01:12:23,637
No. Yes...

1347
01:12:24,013 --> 01:12:25,808
I don't know.

1348
01:12:28,062 --> 01:12:30,358
I just wanted to see if there
was anything left for me here.

1349
01:12:31,653 --> 01:12:32,947
Is there?

1350
01:12:35,912 --> 01:12:37,080
Okay.

1351
01:12:37,080 --> 01:12:39,084
Grace.

1352
01:12:39,084 --> 01:12:41,172
Let her go, man. Let her go,
you've done enough.

1353
01:12:41,172 --> 01:12:44,763
Let's just sit down, have a cup
of hot cocoa and discuss these numbers.

1354
01:12:44,763 --> 01:12:46,558
I think you're gonna be very happy.

1355
01:12:46,558 --> 01:12:49,480
My investors are presenting
a very generous offer,

1356
01:12:49,480 --> 01:12:51,652
all you have to do is sign the papers
and we're good to go.

1357
01:12:51,652 --> 01:12:53,614
Come on, man! This is the best
thing for everyone!

1358
01:12:53,614 --> 01:12:55,701
I should have told you about
Operation Mistletoe.

1359
01:12:58,456 --> 01:13:00,920
I should've told you about
Operation Mistletoe.

1360
01:13:01,337 --> 01:13:02,799
Yeah, you should have.

1361
01:13:03,257 --> 01:13:07,349
I'm sorry, I was just trying to make
this Christmas special for you

1362
01:13:07,349 --> 01:13:09,854
and I was hoping if I got
you and Ryan together,

1363
01:13:09,854 --> 01:13:11,900
that would be enough
to make him stay.

1364
01:13:12,694 --> 01:13:13,696
Guess I was wrong.

1365
01:13:14,488 --> 01:13:16,660
Listen, it's not your fault, okay?

1366
01:13:17,537 --> 01:13:20,125
I'm the one who got wrapped in the idea
of what it would be like

1367
01:13:20,125 --> 01:13:23,089
if Ryan St. Nicholas actually
stayed in Ivy Glen.

1368
01:13:24,592 --> 01:13:28,266
Both of us know that would never happen,
Operation Mistletoe or not.

1369
01:13:29,143 --> 01:13:31,355
I can't believe he's selling
to Quinn.

1370
01:13:31,355 --> 01:13:32,734
I can.

1371
01:13:33,109 --> 01:13:36,073
- You don't mean that.
- No, I do. Quinn was right.

1372
01:13:36,449 --> 01:13:38,537
I got swept up in a fantasy.

1373
01:13:40,791 --> 01:13:43,922
Listen, you're a really good friend,
but lay off the mistletoe for me

1374
01:13:43,922 --> 01:13:46,385
for the foreseeable future.

1375
01:13:46,385 --> 01:13:47,805
I kind of need a break.

1376
01:13:47,805 --> 01:13:50,268
- I can do that.
- Okay.

1377
01:13:54,736 --> 01:13:56,823
How much mistletoe did you have, though?

1378
01:13:56,823 --> 01:13:58,952
So much.

1379
01:14:03,294 --> 01:14:05,173
It's not too bad.

1380
01:14:05,591 --> 01:14:07,302
Okay.

1381
01:14:08,304 --> 01:14:09,808
Oh, still coming.

1382
01:14:09,808 --> 01:14:12,605
And full disclosure, there is some
hanging in your apartment,

1383
01:14:12,605 --> 01:14:15,360
just to be safe.
- Great.

1384
01:14:17,030 --> 01:14:18,449
Are you gonna be okay?

1385
01:14:18,449 --> 01:14:21,497
Yeah, I'm gonna be fine.

1386
01:14:22,875 --> 01:14:24,838
I think.

1387
01:14:25,296 --> 01:14:26,883
Yeah.

1388
01:14:27,802 --> 01:14:29,388
You will.

1389
01:14:40,326 --> 01:14:43,082
Good morning. You can setup
the catering in the kitchen.

1390
01:14:43,082 --> 01:14:44,334
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1391
01:14:44,334 --> 01:14:47,174
There is a row of lights in the sitting
room that still needs to be hung.

1392
01:14:47,174 --> 01:14:48,677
Thank you.

1393
01:14:48,677 --> 01:14:50,263
Thanks.

1394
01:14:51,140 --> 01:14:53,394
Alright.

1395
01:14:56,484 --> 01:14:58,530
Oh, good morning.
- Morning.

1396
01:14:58,530 --> 01:15:00,366
Oh, Olivia, wait. Have you
talked to Grace?

1397
01:15:00,366 --> 01:15:02,496
'Cause she's not answering her phone.

1398
01:15:03,957 --> 01:15:05,293
I think she needs a moment.

1399
01:15:06,796 --> 01:15:09,468
You know, I didn't mean to
lead her on, I just...

1400
01:15:11,347 --> 01:15:13,936
...I didn't realize how much
I enjoyed being with her.

1401
01:15:13,936 --> 01:15:18,110
- Hmm.
- And I know, selfish, guilty.

1402
01:15:18,110 --> 01:15:19,363
Because you're leaving.

1403
01:15:20,448 --> 01:15:23,956
I feel like no matter what
I do, it's the wrong choice.

1404
01:15:27,630 --> 01:15:29,759
Okay. Well, I'm gonna start
setting up for tonight.

1405
01:15:30,844 --> 01:15:32,264
Sorry about the mistletoe.

1406
01:15:32,264 --> 01:15:33,642
- Well,

1407
01:15:33,642 --> 01:15:35,813
I should have realized
it was you.

1408
01:15:53,557 --> 01:15:55,894
(gentle music

1409
01:15:59,151 --> 01:16:02,449
Right there is perfect, thank you.
Thanks, guys.

1410
01:16:02,449 --> 01:16:04,411
Okay.

1411
01:16:46,996 --> 01:16:49,585
Wow! Looks great, thank you.

1412
01:16:49,919 --> 01:16:51,840
It's all Grace.

1413
01:16:51,840 --> 01:16:55,304
Well, we're almost done, so if you want
to head out, I can take care of the rest.

1414
01:16:55,304 --> 01:16:56,683
I'm almost finished.

1415
01:16:59,104 --> 01:17:01,233
You think she's gonna show tonight?

1416
01:17:01,860 --> 01:17:03,697
It's not like Grace to bail
on a commitment.

1417
01:17:05,408 --> 01:17:06,578
I hope you're right.

1418
01:17:10,001 --> 01:17:12,297
You know, if you decided to sell,

1419
01:17:12,297 --> 01:17:15,596
I don't think anyone would blame you,
but just for the record,

1420
01:17:15,596 --> 01:17:17,558
I think we all really enjoyed
having you back.

1421
01:17:42,650 --> 01:17:44,110
Wow.

1422
01:17:44,695 --> 01:17:46,866
Uh...

1423
01:17:48,077 --> 01:17:50,791
Who's there?

1424
01:17:52,460 --> 01:17:54,757
What were you planning on
doing with that?

1425
01:17:54,757 --> 01:17:57,220
Uh... nothing, I don't know.

1426
01:17:57,220 --> 01:18:01,103
I just thought it would...
look better there.

1427
01:18:01,103 --> 01:18:04,317
Okay. Sorry, I didn't mean to scare you,

1428
01:18:04,317 --> 01:18:06,405
I was just making a few last tweaks.

1429
01:18:06,405 --> 01:18:08,702
I wanted to put one more ornament
on the tree.

1430
01:18:09,035 --> 01:18:11,081
Doesn't really go with
the design aesthetic, but okay.

1431
01:18:11,081 --> 01:18:14,045
Well, it happens to be a very
sentimental ornament

1432
01:18:14,045 --> 01:18:16,425
and that's the key to any good design.

1433
01:18:17,010 --> 01:18:18,137
Ryan, I...
- Grace, I...

1434
01:18:19,515 --> 01:18:21,268
Go ahead.

1435
01:18:22,186 --> 01:18:24,357
These last few days have been
amazing.

1436
01:18:25,026 --> 01:18:26,779
It's made me realize how much
of myself

1437
01:18:26,779 --> 01:18:29,535
I've shut off since I've left this place.

1438
01:18:29,535 --> 01:18:33,918
Spending these days with you has kind of
been like my ghost of Christmas past.

1439
01:18:35,212 --> 01:18:38,553
It's made me realize what I want
in my life for my future.

1440
01:18:40,014 --> 01:18:41,475
Which is?

1441
01:18:41,934 --> 01:18:43,772
A life with balance.

1442
01:18:44,899 --> 01:18:47,111
A life spending time
with people I love.

1443
01:18:48,197 --> 01:18:49,992
In a place that...

1444
01:18:50,451 --> 01:18:52,330
feels like home.

1445
01:18:55,671 --> 01:18:57,633
Well, Grace, I...

1446
01:18:57,633 --> 01:19:00,764
I gotta say, I knew you would pull
it off.

1447
01:19:00,764 --> 01:19:03,060
- Pull off what?

1448
01:19:03,060 --> 01:19:05,356
Oh, the event hasn't even started
yet and there's a lineup

1449
01:19:05,356 --> 01:19:07,402
outside of people ready to donate.

1450
01:19:07,402 --> 01:19:10,116
You know, reviving the Ribbons and Bows
Fundraiser

1451
01:19:10,116 --> 01:19:13,122
was a very good plan,
if I do say do myself.

1452
01:19:14,249 --> 01:19:18,257
Oh, and nice tie-in with the tree
in the Time Square, mm, perfect.

1453
01:19:18,257 --> 01:19:20,971
I'm sorry, I'm just so thrilled

1454
01:19:20,971 --> 01:19:23,058
that everything is working out perfectly.

1455
01:19:23,058 --> 01:19:26,440
So, you're not mad about
losing the condo complex?

1456
01:19:26,440 --> 01:19:27,735
What?

1457
01:19:28,068 --> 01:19:29,697
Oh, uh...

1458
01:19:29,697 --> 01:19:31,324
I'm not selling St. Nicholas House.

1459
01:19:31,324 --> 01:19:32,786
You're not?

1460
01:19:32,786 --> 01:19:37,336
No. You were right, it's more
than an asset, it's my legacy.

1461
01:19:38,464 --> 01:19:42,472
I mean, luxury condo complexes are
great to bring in to new residents,

1462
01:19:42,472 --> 01:19:46,313
but I feel like it's more important to
focus on building up

1463
01:19:46,313 --> 01:19:47,900
the community we already have.

1464
01:19:47,900 --> 01:19:50,989
I couldn't agree more,
and if things go smooth today,

1465
01:19:50,989 --> 01:19:53,745
I want to sit down and talk with you about
doing an official partnership

1466
01:19:53,745 --> 01:19:55,874
with Ivy Glen and the St. Nicholas House.

1467
01:19:55,874 --> 01:19:59,422
Oh, now that is something
I could really get behind.

1468
01:20:01,468 --> 01:20:02,554
Oh!

1469
01:20:02,554 --> 01:20:08,525
Oh, Olivia! Grace, I spoke to
the town council and they all agree.

1470
01:20:08,525 --> 01:20:10,862
The example you're setting here
with this fundraiser

1471
01:20:10,862 --> 01:20:12,908
has everyone blown away.
- Oh.

1472
01:20:12,908 --> 01:20:16,122
So, I look forward to hiring Keene
and Rankin

1473
01:20:16,122 --> 01:20:18,795
for all of the city's upcoming
decoration needs.

1474
01:20:18,795 --> 01:20:21,592
Thank you so much!

1475
01:20:21,592 --> 01:20:24,557
Oh, honey, can we check if the greeters
are in place?

1476
01:20:24,557 --> 01:20:28,105
Thank you so much,
because I think it is five o'clock.

1477
01:20:28,105 --> 01:20:29,650
Should we let everyone in?
- Yeah.

1478
01:20:29,650 --> 01:20:32,280
- We got to get this show on the road!
- Let's do it.

1479
01:20:53,155 --> 01:20:56,244
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for coming.

1480
01:20:56,244 --> 01:21:00,294
We wouldn't be here if it weren't
for the generosity of Ryan St. Nicholas.

1481
01:21:00,294 --> 01:21:01,839
So please, Ryan,

1482
01:21:01,839 --> 01:21:03,467
would you do us the honours?
- Of course.

1483
01:21:03,467 --> 01:21:06,891
And first off, big thank you
to Mayor Hoffman for helping convince me

1484
01:21:06,891 --> 01:21:10,230
to do this and all of you for making
this possible.

1485
01:21:10,230 --> 01:21:14,322
As you know, this was
my grandmother's house,

1486
01:21:14,990 --> 01:21:15,992
and in her honour,

1487
01:21:15,992 --> 01:21:20,961
I invite all of you into the Ribbons
and Bows Christmas Fundraiser.

1488
01:21:23,423 --> 01:21:25,804
And none of this would have been
possible

1489
01:21:25,804 --> 01:21:30,354
if it wasn't for the beautiful
artistry of Grace Rankin.

1490
01:21:33,068 --> 01:21:37,828
Oh, and the help of my friends,
Jack and Olivia. Give them a hand.

1491
01:21:40,165 --> 01:21:42,921
Alright, merry Christmas!
Come on in!

1492
01:22:27,719 --> 01:22:30,892
Thank you guys.
Merry Christmas, thank you.

1493
01:22:30,892 --> 01:22:32,394
Merry Christmas.

1494
01:22:33,355 --> 01:22:35,442
I'd say that was a success.

1495
01:22:35,442 --> 01:22:39,075
Yeah, I mean, we raised enough to cover
the food bank,

1496
01:22:39,075 --> 01:22:43,083
the kids after school arts program
and the community centre senior’s events.

1497
01:22:43,083 --> 01:22:45,880
That's amazing!
And a huge thanks to you.

1498
01:22:45,880 --> 01:22:48,678
Well, thank you for being
my ghost of Christmas everything.

1499
01:22:48,678 --> 01:22:51,224
Oh, that's a title I will
gladly accept.

1500
01:22:51,224 --> 01:22:52,936
Okay, I'm gonna go tell Sami.

1501
01:22:52,936 --> 01:22:54,147
Mayor Hoffman.
- Yes.

1502
01:22:54,147 --> 01:22:55,692
- Just call me Sami.
- Oh1

1503
01:22:56,777 --> 01:22:59,490
It's weird having my friends
call me Mayor Hoffman.

1504
01:22:59,490 --> 01:23:02,246
- Thank you so much because honestly,

1505
01:23:02,246 --> 01:23:04,877
I don't know if I was gonna
be able to stick to that.

1506
01:23:05,962 --> 01:23:08,383
Sami, will you please meet me outside?

1507
01:23:08,383 --> 01:23:11,599
I just want to take some formal pictures
while the photographer is still here.

1508
01:23:11,599 --> 01:23:14,103
Absolutely.

1509
01:23:16,316 --> 01:23:19,197
I know that we agreed
I’d lay off the mistletoe,

1510
01:23:19,197 --> 01:23:21,409
but that doesn't mean you have to.

1511
01:23:21,744 --> 01:23:24,207
Merry Christmas.
- Merry Christmas.

1512
01:23:25,710 --> 01:23:28,507
So...

1513
01:23:29,258 --> 01:23:31,471
...what was it you were gonna
say to me earlier?

1514
01:23:33,433 --> 01:23:36,105
I probably should have told
you this back in high school, but...

1515
01:23:36,105 --> 01:23:37,441
What's that?

1516
01:23:37,441 --> 01:23:38,736
I'm in love with you.

1517
01:23:40,280 --> 01:23:41,992
I always have been.

1518
01:23:43,663 --> 01:23:47,294
And you know what? I think
I might stick around for a while.

1519
01:23:48,923 --> 01:23:50,802
Keep my feet on the ground
and who knows,

1520
01:23:50,802 --> 01:23:53,473
maybe wear a t-shirt and jeans
a couple days a week.

1521
01:23:53,473 --> 01:23:54,977
How does that sound?

1522
01:23:54,977 --> 01:23:56,730
Well, what about your clients
in New York?

1523
01:23:56,730 --> 01:24:01,281
Well, I can fly back to New York,
take meetings and do the rest from here.

1524
01:24:01,281 --> 01:24:03,034
- Okay.
- Yeah.

1525
01:24:03,034 --> 01:24:04,997
Then, I just have one last
question for you.

1526
01:24:04,997 --> 01:24:06,457
- What?
- Can you do me a favour?

1527
01:24:06,457 --> 01:24:08,629
Can you hold this up for me?
I'm kind of short.

1528
01:24:08,629 --> 01:24:11,552
- I got you.

1529
01:24:12,136 --> 01:24:14,307
Like that?
- Yeah. You know, apparently,

1530
01:24:14,307 --> 01:24:17,146
it's bad luck if you don't kiss someone
you love under a mistletoe.

1531
01:24:17,146 --> 01:24:19,066
Oh, really?

1532
01:24:19,066 --> 01:24:20,235
Mm-hmm.

1533
01:24:20,235 --> 01:24:22,699
Guess we're gonna have to reinstate
Operation Mistletoe

1534
01:24:22,699 --> 01:24:25,705
'cause we wouldn't want any bad luck
around here, would we?

1535
01:24:25,705 --> 01:24:28,168
- I love you, Ryan St. Nicholas.

1536
01:24:37,061 --> 01:24:38,396
Happy?

1537
01:24:38,396 --> 01:24:40,610
Oh, I am just warming up.

1538
01:24:40,610 --> 01:24:41,654
For what?

1539
01:24:41,654 --> 01:24:43,365
Operation New Year’s Engagement.

1540
01:24:43,365 --> 01:24:44,450
- Yeah.

1541
01:24:46,496 --> 01:24:47,957
Seriously?

1542
01:24:47,957 --> 01:24:50,212
- Oh, yeah.
- No.

1543
01:24:50,212 --> 01:24:53,678
- Yes! Yes!
- I'm not doing that.